# vdom

The retained-tree reconciler every tier renders through. A render writes a flat pre-order TAPE;
`vdCommit` diffs that tape against the retained children of one node and appends the minimal
PATCH STREAM (wire format v2: `Int` words indexing a `Text` string table) a host applies by the
node ids the stream names. The emitter is the id authority: a node keeps its id for its whole
life, and a freed id is reused only after the stream that frees it.

One retained tree serves the whole program, held in module-level `Seq`s: node `n` lives at item
`n + 1` of every node field, children are doubly linked, attributes and listeners sit in pooled
chains with free lists, and every scratch array keeps a logical length, so a steady-state repaint
grows nothing. No `Map` and no record: dense `Int` ids and non-empty-seeded `Seq of Int`/`Seq of
Text` lower alike on every backend.

Node kinds: 1 element, 2 text, 3 fragment (a component boundary with no host node of its own),
4 root (a host node the tree renders into), 0 free. Tape records: 1 OPEN tag key end, 2 TEXT
text, 17 TEXT text site (a text child carrying a site), 3 CLOSE, 5 FRAG_OPEN frag end, 6
FRAG_CLOSE, 7 KEEP frag; an OPEN's modifier run follows it directly: 9 SITE site, 10 ATTR name
value, 11 VALUE value, 12 CHECKED on, 13 LISTEN event flags, 14 HTML html. A caller's children
are drawn where the caller is and placed where the callee says: 15 RANGE end … 16 RANGE_CLOSE
holds them apart from the tape around it, and 8 SLOT range places them; `vdCommit` copies every
range into its slot before anything else reads the tape. A listener or site found for an element
AFTER its open (a sentence naming it by selector) rides beside the tape, keyed by the open's
position (`vdListenAt`/`vdSiteAt`).

A path only some pages take is named for its feature and runs only on a tape holding records the
feature's writers laid down: firm-key checks (`vdKeyed…`, written by `vdOpenKeyed`), matching by
key (`vdKeys…`, by `vdOpenKeyed` and `vdOpenSoft`), range resolution (`vdSlots…`, by `vdRangeOpen`
and `vdSlot`) and hydration (`vdAdopt…`, by `vdHydrate`). The module's dead-code analysis follows a
call into a feature only once one of its writers is reached (`lgx_lower::VDOM_FEATURES`), so a page
that never writes a feature's records ships none of its code.

Auto-imported on reference.

## Main
Let mutable __VD_KIND be [0].
Let mutable __VD_TAG be [""].
Let mutable __VD_TEXT be [""].
Let mutable __VD_HTML be [""].
Let mutable __VD_VALUE be [""].
Let mutable __VD_KEY be [""].
Let mutable __VD_FLAGS be [0].
Let mutable __VD_IDENT be [0].
Let mutable __VD_KH be [0].
Let mutable __VD_PARENT be [-1].
Let mutable __VD_FIRST be [-1].
Let mutable __VD_LAST be [-1].
Let mutable __VD_NEXT be [-1].
Let mutable __VD_PREV be [-1].
Let mutable __VD_ATTR be [0].
Let mutable __VD_LSN be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SITE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_POS be [0].
Let mutable __VD_MARK be [0].
Let mutable __VD_FREE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_FREEN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_LIVE be 0.
Let mutable __VD_AN be [""].
Let mutable __VD_AV be [""].
Let mutable __VD_ANEXT be [0].
Let mutable __VD_AMARK be [0].
Let mutable __VD_AFREE be 0.
Let mutable __VD_LE be [""].
Let mutable __VD_LF be [0].
Let mutable __VD_LNEXT be [0].
Let mutable __VD_LMARK be [0].
Let mutable __VD_LFREE be 0.
Let mutable __VD_FRAGNODE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_WANT be [0].
Let mutable __VD_FRAGFREE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_FRAGFREEN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_GONE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_GONEN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_SITENODE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_TP be [0].
Let mutable __VD_TPN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_TS be [""].
Let mutable __VD_TSN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_OPENS be [0].
Let mutable __VD_ON be 0.
Let mutable __VD_MODOK be 0.
Let mutable __VD_TAPEERR be "".
Let mutable __VD_PW be [0].
Let mutable __VD_PWN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_PS be [""].
Let mutable __VD_PSN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_SERIAL be 0.
Let mutable __VD_MODN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_DIFFN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_R be [0].
Let mutable __VD_F be [0].
Let mutable __VD_M be [0].
Let mutable __VD_KJ be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SEQ be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SEQJ be [0].
Let mutable __VD_LKEEP be [0].
Let mutable __VD_TAILS be [0].
Let mutable __VD_PREVI be [0].
Let mutable __VD_CT be [""].
Let mutable __VD_CP be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SORT be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SORTH be [0].
Let mutable __VD_WP be [0].
Let mutable __VD_WS be [0].
Let mutable __VD_WE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_WN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_DOOM be [0].
Let mutable __VD_DOOMN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_VS be [0].
Let mutable __VD_VE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_VN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_KP be [0].
Let mutable __VD_STK be [0].
Let mutable __VD_STKN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_SN be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SPH be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SNN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_SLOTS be 0.
Let mutable __VD_TQ be [0].
Let mutable __VD_TQN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_RELOC be [0].
Let mutable __VD_RELOCN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_SEGS be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SEGE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SEGN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_SITEFREE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_SITEFREEN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_FRAGANCH be [0].
Let mutable __VD_ANCHSITE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_ANCHNEXT be [0].
Let mutable __VD_ANCHFREE be 0.
Let mutable __VD_ROOTS be [0].
Let mutable __VD_ROOTN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_XP be [0].
Let mutable __VD_XQ be [0].
Let mutable __VD_XOP be [0].
Let mutable __VD_XA be [0].
Let mutable __VD_XB be [0].
Let mutable __VD_XN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_QS be [0].
Let mutable __VD_HYDRATING be 0.
Let mutable __VD_LATE be [0].
Let mutable __VD_LATEN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_STI be [0].
Let mutable __VD_STIN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_STS be [""].
Let mutable __VD_STSN be 0.
Let mutable __VD_STE be [""].
Let mutable __VD_STEN be 0.

## Note
Allocates a node id: the most recently freed one first, else a fresh id one past the end of every node field.

## To vdAlloc() -> Int:
    Set __VD_LIVE to __VD_LIVE + 1.
    If __VD_FREEN > 0:
        Let reused be item __VD_FREEN of __VD_FREE.
        Set __VD_FREEN to __VD_FREEN - 1.
        Return reused.
    Let id be length of __VD_KIND.
    Push 0 to __VD_KIND.
    Push "" to __VD_TAG.
    Push "" to __VD_TEXT.
    Push "" to __VD_HTML.
    Push "" to __VD_VALUE.
    Push "" to __VD_KEY.
    Push 0 to __VD_FLAGS.
    Push 0 to __VD_IDENT.
    Push 0 to __VD_KH.
    Push -1 to __VD_PARENT.
    Push -1 to __VD_FIRST.
    Push -1 to __VD_LAST.
    Push -1 to __VD_NEXT.
    Push -1 to __VD_PREV.
    Push 0 to __VD_ATTR.
    Push 0 to __VD_LSN.
    Push 0 to __VD_SITE.
    Push 0 to __VD_POS.
    Push 0 to __VD_MARK.
    Return id.

## Note
Releases `node`: its attribute and listener chains, its site, a fragment's identity (reported gone), then lists the id for reuse. The caller detached it.

## To vdFree(node: Int):
    Let i be node + 1.
    Let mutable e be item i of __VD_ATTR.
    While e != 0:
        Let nextE be item (e + 1) of __VD_ANEXT.
        vdAttrRelease(e).
        Set e to nextE.
    Set e to item i of __VD_LSN.
    While e != 0:
        Let nextE be item (e + 1) of __VD_LNEXT.
        vdListenRelease(e).
        Set e to nextE.
    Let site be item i of __VD_SITE.
    If site != 0:
        If item (site + 1) of __VD_SITENODE == node:
            Set item (site + 1) of __VD_SITENODE to 0.
    If item i of __VD_KIND == 3:
        Let frag be item i of __VD_IDENT.
        If item (frag + 1) of __VD_FRAGNODE == node:
            Set item (frag + 1) of __VD_FRAGNODE to 0.
            vdPutGone(frag).
    Set item i of __VD_KIND to 0.
    Set item i of __VD_TAG to "".
    Set item i of __VD_TEXT to "".
    Set item i of __VD_HTML to "".
    Set item i of __VD_VALUE to "".
    Set item i of __VD_KEY to "".
    Set item i of __VD_FLAGS to 0.
    Set item i of __VD_IDENT to 0.
    Set item i of __VD_KH to 0.
    Set item i of __VD_PARENT to -1.
    Set item i of __VD_FIRST to -1.
    Set item i of __VD_LAST to -1.
    Set item i of __VD_NEXT to -1.
    Set item i of __VD_PREV to -1.
    Set item i of __VD_ATTR to 0.
    Set item i of __VD_LSN to 0.
    Set item i of __VD_SITE to 0.
    Set item i of __VD_POS to 0.
    Set item i of __VD_MARK to 0.
    Set __VD_FREEN to __VD_FREEN + 1.
    If __VD_FREEN > length of __VD_FREE:
        Push node to __VD_FREE.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_FREEN of __VD_FREE to node.
    Set __VD_LIVE to __VD_LIVE - 1.

## Note
How many nodes are allocated right now — a page's retained tree size, which a steady-state repaint must not grow.

## To vdLiveNodes() -> Int:
    Return __VD_LIVE.

## Note
How many slots every array this module keeps holds in total; a steady-state repaint leaves it unchanged.

## To vdFootprint() -> Int:
    Let nodes be length of __VD_KIND + length of __VD_TAG + length of __VD_TEXT + length of __VD_HTML + length of __VD_VALUE + length of __VD_KEY + length of __VD_FLAGS + length of __VD_IDENT + length of __VD_KH + length of __VD_PARENT + length of __VD_FIRST + length of __VD_LAST + length of __VD_NEXT + length of __VD_PREV + length of __VD_ATTR + length of __VD_LSN + length of __VD_SITE + length of __VD_POS + length of __VD_MARK + length of __VD_FREE.
    Let pools be length of __VD_AN + length of __VD_AV + length of __VD_ANEXT + length of __VD_AMARK + length of __VD_LE + length of __VD_LF + length of __VD_LNEXT + length of __VD_LMARK + length of __VD_FRAGNODE + length of __VD_WANT + length of __VD_FRAGFREE + length of __VD_GONE + length of __VD_SITENODE + length of __VD_SITEFREE + length of __VD_ROOTS + length of __VD_FRAGANCH + length of __VD_ANCHSITE + length of __VD_ANCHNEXT.
    Let tape be length of __VD_TP + length of __VD_TS + length of __VD_OPENS + length of __VD_PW + length of __VD_PS + length of __VD_TQ + length of __VD_RELOC + length of __VD_SEGS + length of __VD_SEGE + length of __VD_XP + length of __VD_XQ + length of __VD_XOP + length of __VD_XA + length of __VD_XB + length of __VD_QS.
    Let scratch be length of __VD_R + length of __VD_F + length of __VD_M + length of __VD_KJ + length of __VD_SEQ + length of __VD_SEQJ + length of __VD_LKEEP + length of __VD_TAILS + length of __VD_PREVI + length of __VD_CT + length of __VD_CP + length of __VD_SORT + length of __VD_SORTH + length of __VD_WP + length of __VD_WS + length of __VD_WE + length of __VD_DOOM + length of __VD_VS + length of __VD_VE + length of __VD_KP + length of __VD_STK + length of __VD_SN + length of __VD_SPH + length of __VD_LATE + length of __VD_STI + length of __VD_STS + length of __VD_STE.
    Return nodes + pools + tape + scratch.

## Note
A new retained root standing for host node `host` (the body is `0`); what `vdCommit` renders into.

## To vdNewRoot(host: Int) -> Int:
    Let node be vdAlloc().
    Set item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND to 4.
    Set item (node + 1) of __VD_IDENT to host.
    Set __VD_ROOTN to __VD_ROOTN + 1.
    If __VD_ROOTN > length of __VD_ROOTS:
        Push node to __VD_ROOTS.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_ROOTN of __VD_ROOTS to node.
    Return node.

## Note
Makes the first commit into fresh root `root` adopt the markup its host already holds (the page's
pre-rendered first paint) instead of creating it.

## To vdHydrate(root: Int):
    Let i be root + 1.
    If ((item i of __VD_FLAGS) & 16) == 0:
        Set item i of __VD_FLAGS to (item i of __VD_FLAGS) + 16.

## Note
Forgets root `root` whole (its retained subtree, its instance fragments, reported gone, and its
pending patch stream) as a render drawn only to be serialized is.

## To vdDiscardRoot(root: Int):
    Let mutable c be item (root + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        Let nextC be item (c + 1) of __VD_NEXT.
        vdDetach(c).
        vdFreeSubtree(c).
        Set c to nextC.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_ROOTN:
        If item k of __VD_ROOTS == root:
            Set item k of __VD_ROOTS to item __VD_ROOTN of __VD_ROOTS.
            Set __VD_ROOTN to __VD_ROOTN - 1.
            Set k to __VD_ROOTN + 1.
        Otherwise:
            Set k to k + 1.
    If __VD_HYDRATING == root:
        Set __VD_HYDRATING to 0.
    vdFree(root).
    vdDropPatches().

## Note
The node the host knows as `wire` — the inverse of `vdWire` — or `-1` when no retained node is.

## To vdNodeOfWire(wire: Int) -> Int:
    If wire >= 2147483648:
        Let node be wire - 2147483648.
        If node >= length of __VD_KIND:
            Return -1.
        If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND == 0:
            Return -1.
        Return node.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_ROOTN:
        Let root be item k of __VD_ROOTS.
        If item (root + 1) of __VD_IDENT == wire:
            Return root.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return -1.

## Note
A site no node carries yet, for `vdSite`/`vdTextSite`/`vdSiteAt` to give one; `vdFreeSite` hands it back.

## To vdNewSite() -> Int:
    If __VD_SITEFREEN > 0:
        Let reused be item __VD_SITEFREEN of __VD_SITEFREE.
        Set __VD_SITEFREEN to __VD_SITEFREEN - 1.
        Return reused.
    Let site be length of __VD_SITENODE.
    Push 0 to __VD_SITENODE.
    Return site.

## Note
Hands `site` back for reuse; the node carrying it, if any, carries none from now on.

## To vdFreeSite(site: Int):
    If site < 1 or site >= length of __VD_SITENODE:
        Return.
    Let node be item (site + 1) of __VD_SITENODE.
    If node != 0:
        If item (node + 1) of __VD_SITE == site:
            Set item (node + 1) of __VD_SITE to 0.
        Set item (site + 1) of __VD_SITENODE to 0.
    Set __VD_SITEFREEN to __VD_SITEFREEN + 1.
    If __VD_SITEFREEN > length of __VD_SITEFREE:
        Push site to __VD_SITEFREE.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_SITEFREEN of __VD_SITEFREE to site.

## Note
Records a site for this paint of instance fragment `frag`, kept in `frag`'s pooled chain until
`vdReleaseAnchors(frag)` hands it back.

## To vdAnchor(frag: Int) -> Int:
    Let site be vdNewSite().
    Let mutable e be __VD_ANCHFREE.
    If e != 0:
        Set __VD_ANCHFREE to item (e + 1) of __VD_ANCHNEXT.
    Otherwise:
        Set e to length of __VD_ANCHSITE.
        Push 0 to __VD_ANCHSITE.
        Push 0 to __VD_ANCHNEXT.
    While length of __VD_FRAGANCH <= frag:
        Push 0 to __VD_FRAGANCH.
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_ANCHSITE to site.
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_ANCHNEXT to item (frag + 1) of __VD_FRAGANCH.
    Set item (frag + 1) of __VD_FRAGANCH to e.
    Return site.

## Note
Hands back every site `vdAnchor` gave fragment `frag`'s instance — what its next paint, or its leaving, does first.

## To vdReleaseAnchors(frag: Int):
    If frag < 1 or frag + 1 > length of __VD_FRAGANCH:
        Return.
    Let mutable e be item (frag + 1) of __VD_FRAGANCH.
    While e != 0:
        vdFreeSite(item (e + 1) of __VD_ANCHSITE).
        Let after be item (e + 1) of __VD_ANCHNEXT.
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_ANCHNEXT to __VD_ANCHFREE.
        Set __VD_ANCHFREE to e.
        Set e to after.
    Set item (frag + 1) of __VD_FRAGANCH to 0.

## Note
The site retained `node` carries, or `0`; `-1` (no node) carries none.

## To vdSiteOf(node: Int) -> Int:
    If node < 0 or node >= length of __VD_KIND:
        Return 0.
    Return item (node + 1) of __VD_SITE.

## Note
The site retained `node` carries, giving it a fresh one when it has none — for a node no tape marks, a root.

## To vdEnsureSite(node: Int) -> Int:
    Let held be item (node + 1) of __VD_SITE.
    If held != 0:
        Return held.
    Let site be vdNewSite().
    Set item (node + 1) of __VD_SITE to site.
    vdPutSiteNode(site, node).
    Return site.

## Note
Writes `text` into retained text `node` in place, as a patch that redraws nothing else would; the stream carries the change.

## To vdPatchText(node: Int, text: Text):
    If node < 1 or node >= length of __VD_KIND:
        Return.
    If item (node + 1) of __VD_TEXT != text:
        Set item (node + 1) of __VD_TEXT to text.
        vdEmitSetText(node, text).

## Note
Writes `value` into retained element `node`'s live value in place.

## To vdPatchValue(node: Int, value: Text):
    If node < 1 or node >= length of __VD_KIND:
        Return.
    Let i be node + 1.
    Let flags be item i of __VD_FLAGS.
    If (flags & 1) == 0 or item i of __VD_VALUE != value:
        vdEmitSetValue(node, value).
    Set item i of __VD_VALUE to value.
    Set item i of __VD_FLAGS to flags | 1.

## Note
Writes `checked` into retained element `node`'s live checked state in place.

## To vdPatchChecked(node: Int, checked: Bool):
    If node < 1 or node >= length of __VD_KIND:
        Return.
    Let i be node + 1.
    Let flags be item i of __VD_FLAGS.
    Let mutable on be 0.
    If checked:
        Set on to 1.
    Let mutable wasOn be 0.
    If (flags & 4) != 0:
        Set wasOn to 1.
    If (flags & 2) == 0 or wasOn != on:
        vdEmitSetChecked(node, on).
    If on == 1:
        Set item i of __VD_FLAGS to flags | 6.
    Otherwise:
        Set item i of __VD_FLAGS to (flags | 2) & 11.

## Note
A fresh fragment identity for one component instance, matched across renders by `vdFragOpen`/`vdKeep`.

## To vdNewFrag() -> Int:
    If __VD_FRAGFREEN > 0:
        Let reused be item __VD_FRAGFREEN of __VD_FRAGFREE.
        Set __VD_FRAGFREEN to __VD_FRAGFREEN - 1.
        Return reused.
    Let frag be length of __VD_FRAGNODE.
    Push 0 to __VD_FRAGNODE.
    Push 0 to __VD_WANT.
    Return frag.

## Note
The retained node fragment `frag` is committed as, or `0` while it is not in the tree.

## To vdFragNode(frag: Int) -> Int:
    If frag < 1 or frag >= length of __VD_FRAGNODE:
        Return 0.
    Return item (frag + 1) of __VD_FRAGNODE.

## Note
The node carrying site `site` after the last commit, or `0` when no retained element carries it.

## To vdSiteNode(site: Int) -> Int:
    If site < 1 or site >= length of __VD_SITENODE:
        Return 0.
    Return item (site + 1) of __VD_SITENODE.

## Note
How many fragments left the tree since `vdClearGone` — the instances whose components were removed.

## To vdGoneCount() -> Int:
    Return __VD_GONEN.

## Note
The `k`-th gone fragment identity, 1-based, in the order the commits removed them.

## To vdGone(k: Int) -> Int:
    Return item k of __VD_GONE.

## Note
Forgets the gone list and hands those fragment identities back to `vdNewFrag` for reuse.

## To vdClearGone():
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_GONEN:
        Let frag be item k of __VD_GONE.
        Set __VD_FRAGFREEN to __VD_FRAGFREEN + 1.
        If __VD_FRAGFREEN > length of __VD_FRAGFREE:
            Push frag to __VD_FRAGFREE.
        Otherwise:
            Set item __VD_FRAGFREEN of __VD_FRAGFREE to frag.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set __VD_GONEN to 0.

## Note
Appends `frag` to the gone list.

## To vdPutGone(frag: Int):
    Set __VD_GONEN to __VD_GONEN + 1.
    If __VD_GONEN > length of __VD_GONE:
        Push frag to __VD_GONE.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_GONEN of __VD_GONE to frag.

## Note
Records `node` as the carrier of site `site`, growing the site table as far as `site` needs.

## To vdPutSiteNode(site: Int, node: Int):
    While length of __VD_SITENODE <= site:
        Push 0 to __VD_SITENODE.
    Set item (site + 1) of __VD_SITENODE to node.

## Note
Takes an attribute pool entry for `name`/`value`, reusing a released one first.

## To vdAttrAlloc(name: Text, value: Text) -> Int:
    If __VD_AFREE != 0:
        Let e be __VD_AFREE.
        Set __VD_AFREE to item (e + 1) of __VD_ANEXT.
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_AN to name.
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_AV to value.
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_ANEXT to 0.
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_AMARK to 0.
        Return e.
    Let e be length of __VD_AN.
    Push name to __VD_AN.
    Push value to __VD_AV.
    Push 0 to __VD_ANEXT.
    Push 0 to __VD_AMARK.
    Return e.

## Note
Returns attribute pool entry `e` to the free chain.

## To vdAttrRelease(e: Int):
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_AN to "".
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_AV to "".
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_AMARK to 0.
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_ANEXT to __VD_AFREE.
    Set __VD_AFREE to e.

## Note
Takes a listener pool entry for `event`/`flags`, reusing a released one first.

## To vdListenAlloc(event: Text, flags: Int) -> Int:
    If __VD_LFREE != 0:
        Let e be __VD_LFREE.
        Set __VD_LFREE to item (e + 1) of __VD_LNEXT.
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LE to event.
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LF to flags.
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LNEXT to 0.
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LMARK to 0.
        Return e.
    Let e be length of __VD_LE.
    Push event to __VD_LE.
    Push flags to __VD_LF.
    Push 0 to __VD_LNEXT.
    Push 0 to __VD_LMARK.
    Return e.

## Note
Returns listener pool entry `e` to the free chain.

## To vdListenRelease(e: Int):
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LE to "".
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LF to 0.
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LMARK to 0.
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LNEXT to __VD_LFREE.
    Set __VD_LFREE to e.

## Note
Removes `node` from its parent's child list; `node` and its own children stay intact.

## To vdDetach(node: Int):
    Let i be node + 1.
    Let parent be item i of __VD_PARENT.
    If parent == -1:
        Return.
    Let prev be item i of __VD_PREV.
    Let next be item i of __VD_NEXT.
    If prev == -1:
        Set item (parent + 1) of __VD_FIRST to next.
    Otherwise:
        Set item (prev + 1) of __VD_NEXT to next.
    If next == -1:
        Set item (parent + 1) of __VD_LAST to prev.
    Otherwise:
        Set item (next + 1) of __VD_PREV to prev.
    Set item i of __VD_PARENT to -1.
    Set item i of __VD_PREV to -1.
    Set item i of __VD_NEXT to -1.

## Note
True unless `node` is a fragment — the one kind with no host node of its own.

## To vdIsReal(node: Int) -> Bool:
    Return item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3.

## Note
`node` itself when it has a host node, else its nearest ancestor that does, or `-1` when it hangs from nothing.

## To vdRealOf(node: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable n be node.
    While item (n + 1) of __VD_KIND == 3:
        Let up be item (n + 1) of __VD_PARENT.
        If up == -1:
            Return -1.
        Set n to up.
    Return n.

## Note
The id the host knows `node` by: a root's own host node, every other node its id in the stream range from 2^31 up, where a host mints none of its own.

## To vdWire(node: Int) -> Int:
    If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND == 4:
        Return item (node + 1) of __VD_IDENT.
    Return node + 2147483648.

## Note
The node after `c` in a pre-order walk that skips `c`'s own subtree and never leaves `top`, or `-1`.

## To vdAfter(c: Int, top: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable n be c.
    While n != top:
        Let s be item (n + 1) of __VD_NEXT.
        If s != -1:
            Return s.
        Set n to item (n + 1) of __VD_PARENT.
    Return -1.

## Note
The first node with a host node at or under `node`, in document order, or `-1` for an empty fragment.

## To vdFirstReal(node: Int) -> Int:
    If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
        Return node.
    Let mutable c be item (node + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        If item (c + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
            Return c.
        Let down be item (c + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
        If down != -1:
            Set c to down.
        Otherwise:
            Set c to vdAfter(c, node).
    Return -1.

## Note
The first host node after fragment `node`'s own range under its real parent, or `-1` when the range ends that parent.

## To vdAnchorAfter(node: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable n be node.
    While item (n + 1) of __VD_KIND == 3:
        Let mutable s be item (n + 1) of __VD_NEXT.
        While s != -1:
            Let first be vdFirstReal(s).
            If first != -1:
                Return first.
            Set s to item (s + 1) of __VD_NEXT.
        Set n to item (n + 1) of __VD_PARENT.
        If n == -1:
            Return -1.
    Return -1.

## Note
Appends word `v` to the pending patch stream.

## To vdEmitInt(v: Int):
    Set __VD_PWN to __VD_PWN + 1.
    If __VD_PWN > length of __VD_PW:
        Push v to __VD_PW.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_PWN of __VD_PW to v.

## Note
Appends `s` to the pending stream's string table and returns its 1-based position there.

## To vdEmitStr(s: Text) -> Int:
    Set __VD_PSN to __VD_PSN + 1.
    If __VD_PSN > length of __VD_PS:
        Push s to __VD_PS.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_PSN of __VD_PS to s.
    Return __VD_PSN.

## Note
Emits `CreateElement(node, tag)` (wire opcode 1).

## To vdEmitCreateElement(node: Int, tag: Text):
    vdEmitInt(1).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(tag)).

## Note
Emits `CreateTextNode(node, text)` (wire opcode 2).

## To vdEmitCreateText(node: Int, text: Text):
    vdEmitInt(2).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(text)).

## Note
Emits `SetText(node, text)` (wire opcode 3).

## To vdEmitSetText(node: Int, text: Text):
    vdEmitInt(3).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(text)).

## Note
Emits `SetHtml(node, markup)` (wire opcode 4).

## To vdEmitSetHtml(node: Int, markup: Text):
    vdEmitInt(4).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(markup)).

## Note
Emits `SetAttribute(node, name, value)` (wire opcode 6).

## To vdEmitSetAttribute(node: Int, name: Text, value: Text):
    vdEmitInt(6).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(name)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(value)).

## Note
Emits `AppendChild(parent, child)` (wire opcode 7).

## To vdEmitAppendChild(parent: Int, child: Int):
    vdEmitInt(7).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(parent)).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(child)).

## Note
Emits `SetValue(node, value)` (wire opcode 8).

## To vdEmitSetValue(node: Int, value: Text):
    vdEmitInt(8).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(value)).

## Note
Emits `SetChecked(node, on)` (wire opcode 9).

## To vdEmitSetChecked(node: Int, on: Int):
    vdEmitInt(9).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(on).

## Note
Emits `InsertBefore(parent, child, before)` (wire opcode 15); `before` is `-1` to append, which the wire spells `u32::MAX`.

## To vdEmitInsertBefore(parent: Int, child: Int, before: Int):
    vdEmitInt(15).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(parent)).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(child)).
    If before == -1:
        vdEmitInt(4294967295).
    Otherwise:
        vdEmitInt(vdWire(before)).

## Note
Emits `RemoveAttribute(node, name)` (wire opcode 16).

## To vdEmitRemoveAttribute(node: Int, name: Text):
    vdEmitInt(16).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(name)).

## Note
Emits `Listen(node, event, flags)` (wire opcode 19).

## To vdEmitListen(node: Int, event: Text, flags: Int):
    vdEmitInt(19).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(event)).
    vdEmitInt(flags).

## Note
Emits `Unlisten(node, event)` (wire opcode 20).

## To vdEmitUnlisten(node: Int, event: Text):
    vdEmitInt(20).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(event)).

## Note
Emits `FreeNode(node)` (wire opcode 21): the host detaches it and forgets it and every descendant.

## To vdEmitFreeNode(node: Int):
    vdEmitInt(21).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).

## Note
Emits `Adopt(parent, node, tag)` (wire opcode 17): the host binds `node` to the next element of `tag` its markup holds under `parent`.

## To vdAdoptEmitElement(parent: Int, node: Int, tag: Text):
    vdEmitInt(17).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(parent)).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(tag)).

## Note
Emits `AdoptText(parent, node, text)` (wire opcode 18): the host binds `node` to its place in the markup's text under `parent`.

## To vdAdoptEmitText(parent: Int, node: Int, text: Text):
    vdEmitInt(18).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(parent)).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(node)).
    vdEmitInt(vdEmitStr(text)).

## Note
Emits `Hydrate(root)` (wire opcode 22): the stream's claims adopt the markup `root`'s host node holds.

## To vdAdoptEmitHydrate(root: Int):
    vdEmitInt(22).
    vdEmitInt(vdWire(root)).

## Note
Emits `SetValue(node, value)` — for a `<select>`, once the commit has placed every option it can choose from, since a browser's select takes only a value one of its options offers.

## To vdSetValueOf(node: Int, value: Text):
    If item (node + 1) of __VD_TAG != "select":
        vdEmitSetValue(node, value).
        Return.
    Set __VD_LATEN to __VD_LATEN + 1.
    If __VD_LATEN > length of __VD_LATE:
        Push node to __VD_LATE.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_LATEN of __VD_LATE to node.

## Note
Emits the values `vdSetValueOf` held back for the `<select>`s this commit wrote, their options now in place.

## To vdEmitLate():
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_LATEN:
        Let node be item k of __VD_LATE.
        vdEmitSetValue(node, item (node + 1) of __VD_VALUE).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set __VD_LATEN to 0.

## Note
Emits every write retained element `node` carries — its attributes, value, checked state, raw markup and listeners.

## To vdAdoptState(node: Int):
    Let i be node + 1.
    Let mutable e be item i of __VD_ATTR.
    While e != 0:
        vdEmitSetAttribute(node, item (e + 1) of __VD_AN, item (e + 1) of __VD_AV).
        Set e to item (e + 1) of __VD_ANEXT.
    Let flags be item i of __VD_FLAGS.
    If (flags & 1) != 0:
        vdSetValueOf(node, item i of __VD_VALUE).
    If (flags & 2) != 0:
        If (flags & 4) != 0:
            vdEmitSetChecked(node, 1).
        Otherwise:
            vdEmitSetChecked(node, 0).
    If item i of __VD_HTML != "":
        vdEmitSetHtml(node, item i of __VD_HTML).
    Set e to item i of __VD_LSN.
    While e != 0:
        vdEmitListen(node, item (e + 1) of __VD_LE, item (e + 1) of __VD_LF).
        Set e to item (e + 1) of __VD_LNEXT.

## Note
Emits root `root`'s retained subtree in document order: with `adopt`, a claim per node for the host
to bind its markup; without, a create, the writes and an append per node.

## To vdAdoptTree(root: Int, adopt: Bool):
    If adopt:
        vdAdoptEmitHydrate(root).
    Let mutable n be item (root + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While n != -1:
        Let i be n + 1.
        Let kind be item i of __VD_KIND.
        Let host be vdRealOf(item i of __VD_PARENT).
        Let mutable descend be true.
        If kind == 1:
            If adopt:
                vdAdoptEmitElement(host, n, item i of __VD_TAG).
            Otherwise:
                vdEmitCreateElement(n, item i of __VD_TAG).
            vdAdoptState(n).
            If not adopt:
                vdEmitAppendChild(host, n).
            If item i of __VD_HTML != "":
                Set descend to false.
        Otherwise If kind == 2:
            If adopt:
                vdAdoptEmitText(host, n, item i of __VD_TEXT).
            Otherwise:
                vdEmitCreateText(n, item i of __VD_TEXT).
                vdEmitAppendChild(host, n).
        Let mutable next be -1.
        If descend:
            Set next to item i of __VD_FIRST.
        If next == -1:
            Set next to vdAfter(n, root).
        Set n to next.
    vdEmitLate().

## Note
How many words the pending patch stream holds.

## To vdPatchLength() -> Int:
    Return __VD_PWN.

## Note
A copy of the pending patch stream's words — what a host decodes against `vdPatchStrings`.

## To vdPatchWords() -> Seq of Int:
    Let out be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_PWN:
        Push (item k of __VD_PW) to out.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return out.

## Note
A copy of the pending patch stream's string table; a word naming text holds a 1-based position into it.

## To vdPatchStrings() -> Seq of Text:
    Let out be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_PSN:
        Push (item k of __VD_PS) to out.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return out.

## Note
Forgets the pending patch stream, as a host does once it has applied it.

## To vdDropPatches():
    Set __VD_PWN to 0.
    Set __VD_PSN to 0.

## Note
Hands the pending patch stream to the page's host in one call and forgets it; answers how many of a
hydration's claims found no markup to bind.

## To vdApply() -> Int:
    Let mismatches be applyPatchWords(__VD_PW, __VD_PWN, __VD_PS, __VD_PSN).
    vdDropPatches().
    If __VD_HYDRATING == 0:
        Return mismatches.
    Return vdAdoptSettle(mismatches).

## Note
Ends the hydration the stream just applied: when claims found no markup, the host frees what it
bound and the root is drawn afresh. Answers the mismatches.

## To vdAdoptSettle(mismatches: Int) -> Int:
    Let root be __VD_HYDRATING.
    Set __VD_HYDRATING to 0.
    If mismatches == 0:
        Return 0.
    Let mutable c be item (root + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        vdEmitFreeTops(c).
        Set c to item (c + 1) of __VD_NEXT.
    vdAdoptTree(root, false).
    Let redrawn be applyPatchWords(__VD_PW, __VD_PWN, __VD_PS, __VD_PSN).
    vdDropPatches().
    Return mismatches + redrawn.

## Note
Appends word `v` to the tape being rendered.

## To vdTapeInt(v: Int):
    Set __VD_TPN to __VD_TPN + 1.
    If __VD_TPN > length of __VD_TP:
        Push v to __VD_TP.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_TPN of __VD_TP to v.

## Note
Appends `s` to the tape's string table and returns its 1-based position there.

## To vdTapeStr(s: Text) -> Int:
    Set __VD_TSN to __VD_TSN + 1.
    If __VD_TSN > length of __VD_TS:
        Push s to __VD_TS.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_TSN of __VD_TS to s.
    Return __VD_TSN.

## Note
How many words the tape being rendered holds.

## To vdTapeLength() -> Int:
    Return __VD_TPN.

## Note
The tape word at 1-based position `p`.

## To vdTapeItem(p: Int) -> Int:
    Return item p of __VD_TP.

## Note
Records the first thing wrong with the tape being rendered; `vdCommit` refuses it by this message.

## To vdTapeFault(message: Text):
    If __VD_TAPEERR == "":
        Set __VD_TAPEERR to message.

## Note
Pushes the 1-based tape position of the OPEN or FRAG_OPEN record now open.

## To vdPushOpen(p: Int):
    Set __VD_ON to __VD_ON + 1.
    If __VD_ON > length of __VD_OPENS:
        Push p to __VD_OPENS.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_ON of __VD_OPENS to p.

## Note
Opens an unkeyed element `tag`.

## To vdOpen(tag: Text):
    Let tagIdx be vdTapeStr(tag).
    vdOpenRecord(tagIdx, vdTapeStr("")).

## Note
Opens element `tag` identified among its siblings by `key` (a `keyed by` row), reused across renders by that key.

## To vdOpenKeyed(tag: Text, key: Text):
    Let tagIdx be vdTapeStr(tag).
    vdOpenRecord(tagIdx, vdTapeStr(key)).

## Note
Opens element `tag` identified among its siblings by `key` (an element's `id`): matched across
renders like `vdOpenKeyed`, but a repeated key draws the later sibling fresh.

## To vdOpenSoft(tag: Text, key: Text):
    Let tagIdx be vdTapeStr(tag).
    vdOpenRecord(tagIdx, 0 - vdTapeStr(key)).

## Note
Writes an OPEN record for the tag at string `tagIdx` with key slot `keySlot` — a key string's index, negated for a key that is the element's own identity — and makes it the open element.

## To vdOpenRecord(tagIdx: Int, keySlot: Int):
    vdTapeInt(1).
    Let at be __VD_TPN.
    vdTapeInt(tagIdx).
    vdTapeInt(keySlot).
    vdTapeInt(0).
    vdPushOpen(at).
    Set __VD_MODOK to 1.

## Note
Closes the element `vdOpen`/`vdOpenKeyed` opened last, recording where it ends.

## To vdClose():
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    If __VD_ON == 0:
        vdTapeFault("vdom: vdClose with no element open").
        Return.
    Let p be item __VD_ON of __VD_OPENS.
    If item p of __VD_TP != 1:
        vdTapeFault("vdom: vdClose would close a fragment; a fragment ends with vdFragClose").
        Return.
    Set __VD_ON to __VD_ON - 1.
    vdTapeInt(3).
    Set item (p + 3) of __VD_TP to __VD_TPN.

## Note
Appends a text child `text`.

## To vdText(text: Text):
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    Let textIdx be vdTapeStr(text).
    vdTapeInt(2).
    vdTapeInt(textIdx).

## Note
Appends a text child `text` carrying `site`, so `vdSiteNode(site)` finds its node after the commit.

## To vdTextSite(text: Text, site: Int):
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    Let textIdx be vdTapeStr(text).
    vdTapeInt(17).
    vdTapeInt(textIdx).
    vdTapeInt(site).

## Note
Opens a detached range for a caller's children: drawn here, placed where a `vdSlot` of the returned position says.

## To vdRangeOpen() -> Int:
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    vdTapeInt(15).
    Let at be __VD_TPN.
    vdTapeInt(0).
    vdPushOpen(at).
    Set __VD_SLOTS to __VD_SLOTS + 1.
    Return at.

## Note
Closes the range `vdRangeOpen` opened last.

## To vdRangeClose():
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    If __VD_ON == 0:
        vdTapeFault("vdom: vdRangeClose with no range open").
        Return.
    Let p be item __VD_ON of __VD_OPENS.
    If item p of __VD_TP != 15:
        vdTapeFault("vdom: vdRangeClose would close an element or a fragment").
        Return.
    Set __VD_ON to __VD_ON - 1.
    vdTapeInt(16).
    Set item (p + 1) of __VD_TP to __VD_TPN.

## Note
Places the range opened at tape position `range` here, as this position's children.

## To vdSlot(range: Int):
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    vdTapeInt(8).
    vdTapeInt(range).
    Set __VD_SLOTS to __VD_SLOTS + 1.

## Note
Opens the boundary of component instance `frag` (from `vdNewFrag`), matched across renders by that identity.

## To vdFragOpen(frag: Int):
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    vdTapeInt(5).
    Let at be __VD_TPN.
    vdTapeInt(frag).
    vdTapeInt(0).
    vdPushOpen(at).

## Note
Closes the fragment `vdFragOpen` opened last, recording where it ends.

## To vdFragClose():
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    If __VD_ON == 0:
        vdTapeFault("vdom: vdFragClose with no fragment open").
        Return.
    Let p be item __VD_ON of __VD_OPENS.
    If item p of __VD_TP != 5:
        vdTapeFault("vdom: vdFragClose would close an element; an element ends with vdClose").
        Return.
    Set __VD_ON to __VD_ON - 1.
    vdTapeInt(6).
    Set item (p + 2) of __VD_TP to __VD_TPN.

## Note
Places retained fragment `frag` unchanged — its instance did not re-render — wherever the tree last held it.

## To vdKeep(frag: Int):
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    vdTapeInt(7).
    vdTapeInt(frag).

## Note
Refuses a modifier written anywhere but straight after its element's open.

## To vdModifierAllowed(what: Text) -> Bool:
    If __VD_MODOK == 1:
        Return true.
    vdTapeFault("vdom: " + what + " must follow its element's vdOpen, before any child").
    Return false.

## Note
Marks the element just opened with site `site`, so `vdSiteNode(site)` finds its node after the commit.

## To vdSite(site: Int):
    If vdModifierAllowed("vdSite"):
        vdTapeInt(9).
        vdTapeInt(site).

## Note
Sets attribute `name` to `value` on the element just opened.

## To vdSetAttribute(name: Text, value: Text):
    If vdModifierAllowed("vdSetAttribute"):
        Let nameIdx be vdTapeStr(name).
        Let valueIdx be vdTapeStr(value).
        vdTapeInt(10).
        vdTapeInt(nameIdx).
        vdTapeInt(valueIdx).

## Note
Binds `value` as the live `value` property of the element just opened.

## To vdSetValue(value: Text):
    If vdModifierAllowed("vdSetValue"):
        Let valueIdx be vdTapeStr(value).
        vdTapeInt(11).
        vdTapeInt(valueIdx).

## Note
Binds `checked` as the live checked state of the element just opened.

## To vdSetChecked(checked: Bool):
    If vdModifierAllowed("vdSetChecked"):
        vdTapeInt(12).
        If checked:
            vdTapeInt(1).
        Otherwise:
            vdTapeInt(0).

## Note
Listens for `event` on the element just opened, with its behaviour `flags` (prevent 1, stop 2, capture 8, passive 16).

## To vdListen(event: Text, flags: Int):
    If vdModifierAllowed("vdListen"):
        Let eventIdx be vdTapeStr(event).
        vdTapeInt(13).
        vdTapeInt(eventIdx).
        vdTapeInt(flags).

## Note
Gives the element just opened raw `markup` as its whole content; it takes no children of its own.

## To vdSetHtml(markup: Text):
    If vdModifierAllowed("vdSetHtml"):
        Let htmlIdx be vdTapeStr(markup).
        vdTapeInt(14).
        vdTapeInt(htmlIdx).

## Note
Records a side modifier `op` (13 LISTEN, 9 SITE) for the OPEN at tape position `p`, with its operands.

## To vdPutSide(p: Int, op: Int, a: Int, b: Int):
    Set __VD_XN to __VD_XN + 1.
    If __VD_XN > length of __VD_XP:
        Push p to __VD_XP.
        Push 0 to __VD_XQ.
        Push op to __VD_XOP.
        Push a to __VD_XA.
        Push b to __VD_XB.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_XN of __VD_XP to p.
        Set item __VD_XN of __VD_XQ to 0.
        Set item __VD_XN of __VD_XOP to op.
        Set item __VD_XN of __VD_XA to a.
        Set item __VD_XN of __VD_XB to b.

## Note
Listens for `event` with `flags` on the element OPENed at tape position `p`, found after its open.

## To vdListenAt(p: Int, event: Text, flags: Int):
    If p < 1 or p > __VD_TPN or item p of __VD_TP != 1:
        vdTapeFault("vdom: vdListenAt names tape position " + "{p}" + ", which is no element's open").
        Return.
    vdPutSide(p, 13, vdTapeStr(event), flags).

## Note
Marks the element OPENed at tape position `p` with `site`, found after its open.

## To vdSiteAt(p: Int, site: Int):
    If p < 1 or p > __VD_TPN or item p of __VD_TP != 1:
        vdTapeFault("vdom: vdSiteAt names tape position " + "{p}" + ", which is no element's open").
        Return.
    vdPutSide(p, 9, site, 0).

## Note
The site the OPEN at tape position `p` carries — its own SITE modifier or one beside the tape — or `0`.

## To vdTapeSite(p: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable c be p + 4.
    Let mutable more be true.
    While more:
        Let op be item c of __VD_TP.
        If op == 9:
            Return item (c + 1) of __VD_TP.
        If op == 10 or op == 13:
            Set c to c + 3.
        Otherwise If op == 11 or op == 12 or op == 14:
            Set c to c + 2.
        Otherwise:
            Set more to false.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_XN:
        If item k of __VD_XP == p and item k of __VD_XOP == 9:
            Return item k of __VD_XA.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return 0.

## Note
The tape position of the ATTR record named `name` in the modifier run of the OPEN at position `p`, or `0`.

## To vdOpenAttr(p: Int, name: Text) -> Int:
    Let mutable c be p + 4.
    Let mutable more be true.
    While more:
        Let op be item c of __VD_TP.
        If op == 10:
            If item (item (c + 1) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS == name:
                Return c.
            Set c to c + 3.
        Otherwise If op == 13:
            Set c to c + 3.
        Otherwise If op == 9 or op == 11 or op == 12 or op == 14:
            Set c to c + 2.
        Otherwise:
            Set more to false.
    Return 0.

## Note
True when every space-separated word of `wanted` is a word of `have`, compared byte for byte.

## To vdWordsIn(wanted: Text, have: Text) -> Bool:
    Let want be text_bytes(wanted).
    Let wn be length of want.
    Let held be text_bytes(have).
    Let hn be length of held.
    Let mutable at be 1.
    While at <= wn:
        Let mutable stop be at.
        While stop <= wn and item stop of want != 32:
            Set stop to stop + 1.
        If stop > at:
            Let width be stop - at.
            Let mutable found be false.
            Let mutable h be 1.
            While not found and h <= hn:
                Let mutable hs be h.
                While hs <= hn and item hs of held != 32:
                    Set hs to hs + 1.
                If hs - h == width:
                    Let mutable same be true.
                    Let mutable k be 0.
                    While same and k < width:
                        If item (at + k) of want != item (h + k) of held:
                            Set same to false.
                        Set k to k + 1.
                    If same:
                        Set found to true.
                Set h to hs + 1.
            If not found:
                Return false.
        Set at to stop + 1.
    Return true.

## Note
True when compound `i` of a selector holds of the element OPENed at tape position `p`: its tag (any case), its id, every class, every attribute (present, or equal when `attrValued` says so).

## To vdCompoundHolds(p: Int, i: Int, tags: Seq of Text, ids: Seq of Text, classes: Seq of Text, attrFrom: Seq of Int, attrNames: Seq of Text, attrValues: Seq of Text, attrValued: Seq of Int) -> Bool:
    Let tag be item i of tags.
    If tag != "" and not vdTagIn(vdTapeTag(p), tag):
        Return false.
    Let id be item i of ids.
    If id != "":
        Let a be vdOpenAttr(p, "id").
        If a == 0:
            Return false.
        If item (item (a + 2) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS != id:
            Return false.
    Let wanted be item i of classes.
    If wanted != "":
        Let a be vdOpenAttr(p, "class").
        If a == 0:
            Return false.
        If not vdWordsIn(wanted, item (item (a + 2) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS):
            Return false.
    Let mutable j be item i of attrFrom.
    Let last be item (i + 1) of attrFrom.
    While j < last:
        Let a be vdOpenAttr(p, item j of attrNames).
        If a == 0:
            Return false.
        If item j of attrValued == 1:
            If item (item (a + 2) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS != item j of attrValues:
                Return false.
        Set j to j + 1.
    Return true.

## Note
The tape position of the first element, from `from` on, that a parsed selector's compound chain
names, or `0`: what `querySelector` answers, asked of the tape.

## To vdQuery(from: Int, tags: Seq of Text, ids: Seq of Text, classes: Seq of Text, attrFrom: Seq of Int, attrNames: Seq of Text, attrValues: Seq of Text, attrValued: Seq of Int) -> Int:
    Let n be length of tags.
    Let mutable depth be 0.
    Let mutable p be from.
    While p <= __VD_TPN:
        Let op be item p of __VD_TP.
        If op == 1:
            If vdCompoundHolds(p, n, tags, ids, classes, attrFrom, attrNames, attrValues, attrValued):
                Let mutable i be n - 1.
                Let mutable a be depth.
                While i >= 1 and a >= 1:
                    If vdCompoundHolds(item a of __VD_QS, i, tags, ids, classes, attrFrom, attrNames, attrValues, attrValued):
                        Set i to i - 1.
                    Set a to a - 1.
                If i < 1:
                    Return p.
            Set depth to depth + 1.
            If depth > length of __VD_QS:
                Push p to __VD_QS.
            Otherwise:
                Set item depth of __VD_QS to p.
        Otherwise If op == 3:
            If depth > 0:
                Set depth to depth - 1.
        Set p to vdTapeSkipRecord(p).
    Return 0.

## Note
The characters `from` up to `to` (exclusive) of `chars`, joined, with any quote or space trimmed from both ends.

## To vdCharsText(chars: Seq of Text, from: Int, to: Int) -> Text:
    Let mutable lo be from.
    Let mutable hi be to.
    While lo < hi and (item lo of chars == " " or item lo of chars == "\"" or item lo of chars == "'"):
        Set lo to lo + 1.
    While hi > lo and (item (hi - 1) of chars == " " or item (hi - 1) of chars == "\"" or item (hi - 1) of chars == "'"):
        Set hi to hi - 1.
    Let mutable out be "".
    Let mutable k be lo.
    While k < hi:
        Set out to out + item k of chars.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return out.

## Note
`vdQuery` for a selector given as text, parsed as `lgx::selector` parses it, or `0` for one outside
that subset (a combinator, a list, a pseudo-class, `*`).

## To vdQueryText(from: Int, sel: Text) -> Int:
    Let mutable chars be a new Seq of Text.
    For each ch in sel:
        Push ch to chars.
    Let n be length of chars.
    Let mutable bracket be false.
    Let mutable c be 1.
    While c <= n:
        Let x be item c of chars.
        If x == "[":
            Set bracket to true.
        Otherwise If x == "]":
            Set bracket to false.
        Otherwise If not bracket and (x == ">" or x == "+" or x == "~" or x == "," or x == ":" or x == "*"):
            Return 0.
        Set c to c + 1.
    Let mutable tags be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable ids be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable classes be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable attrFrom be [1].
    Let mutable attrNames be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable attrValues be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable attrValued be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i <= n:
        While i <= n and item i of chars == " ":
            Set i to i + 1.
        If i <= n:
            Let start be i.
            While i <= n and item i of chars != " ":
                Set i to i + 1.
            Let stop be i.
            Let mutable j be start.
            While j < stop and item j of chars != "#" and item j of chars != "." and item j of chars != "[":
                Set j to j + 1.
            Let mutable tag be "".
            Let mutable t be start.
            While t < j:
                Set tag to tag + vdLowerChar(item t of chars).
                Set t to t + 1.
            Push tag to tags.
            Let mutable id be "".
            Let mutable wanted be "".
            Let attrsBefore be length of attrNames.
            While j < stop:
                Let mark be item j of chars.
                If mark == "#" or mark == ".":
                    Let nameFrom be j + 1.
                    Set j to j + 1.
                    While j < stop and item j of chars != "#" and item j of chars != "." and item j of chars != "[":
                        Set j to j + 1.
                    If j == nameFrom:
                        Return 0.
                    Let name be vdCharsText(chars, nameFrom, j).
                    If mark == "#":
                        Set id to name.
                    Otherwise If wanted == "":
                        Set wanted to name.
                    Otherwise:
                        Set wanted to wanted + " " + name.
                Otherwise If mark == "[":
                    Let innerFrom be j + 1.
                    Set j to j + 1.
                    While j < stop and item j of chars != "]":
                        Set j to j + 1.
                    If j >= stop:
                        Return 0.
                    Let mutable eq be innerFrom.
                    While eq < j and item eq of chars != "=":
                        Set eq to eq + 1.
                    If eq < j:
                        Push vdCharsText(chars, innerFrom, eq) to attrNames.
                        Push vdCharsText(chars, eq + 1, j) to attrValues.
                        Push 1 to attrValued.
                    Otherwise:
                        Push vdCharsText(chars, innerFrom, j) to attrNames.
                        Push "" to attrValues.
                        Push 0 to attrValued.
                    Set j to j + 1.
                Otherwise:
                    Return 0.
            If tag == "" and id == "" and wanted == "" and length of attrNames == attrsBefore:
                Return 0.
            Push id to ids.
            Push wanted to classes.
            Push length of attrNames + 1 to attrFrom.
    If length of tags == 0:
        Return 0.
    Return vdQuery(from, tags, ids, classes, attrFrom, attrNames, attrValues, attrValued).

## Note
`ch` in lower case when it is an ASCII capital, else `ch` itself.

## To vdLowerChar(ch: Text) -> Text:
    Let caps be "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ".
    Let small be "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz".
    Let mutable k be 1.
    For each c in caps:
        If c == ch:
            Let mutable m be 1.
            For each s in small:
                If m == k:
                    Return s.
                Set m to m + 1.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return ch.

## Note
Appends word `v` to the stash's int words.

## To vdStashInt(v: Int):
    Set __VD_STIN to __VD_STIN + 1.
    If __VD_STIN > length of __VD_STI:
        Push v to __VD_STI.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_STIN of __VD_STI to v.

## Note
Appends `s` to the stash's text words.

## To vdStashStr(s: Text):
    Set __VD_STSN to __VD_STSN + 1.
    If __VD_STSN > length of __VD_STS:
        Push s to __VD_STS.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_STSN of __VD_STS to s.

## Note
Moves the tape in flight aside and leaves an empty one, for a render drawn inside another; answers
the handle `vdTapeUnstash` restores it by.

## To vdTapeStash() -> Int:
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_TPN:
        vdStashInt(item k of __VD_TP).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= __VD_ON:
        vdStashInt(item k of __VD_OPENS).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= __VD_XN:
        vdStashInt(item k of __VD_XP).
        vdStashInt(item k of __VD_XOP).
        vdStashInt(item k of __VD_XA).
        vdStashInt(item k of __VD_XB).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= __VD_PWN:
        vdStashInt(item k of __VD_PW).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= __VD_TSN:
        vdStashStr(item k of __VD_TS).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= __VD_PSN:
        vdStashStr(item k of __VD_PS).
        Set k to k + 1.
    vdStashInt(__VD_TPN).
    vdStashInt(__VD_ON).
    vdStashInt(__VD_XN).
    vdStashInt(__VD_PWN).
    vdStashInt(__VD_TSN).
    vdStashInt(__VD_PSN).
    vdStashInt(__VD_MODOK).
    vdStashInt(__VD_SLOTS).
    vdStashInt(__VD_HYDRATING).
    vdStashStr(__VD_TAPEERR).
    Set __VD_STEN to __VD_STEN + 1.
    vdAbort().
    vdDropPatches().
    Set __VD_HYDRATING to 0.
    Return __VD_STEN.

## Note
Puts back the tape `vdTapeStash` moved aside under `handle` — the last one stashed — exactly as it was, discarding whatever tape and stream are in flight.

## To vdTapeUnstash(handle: Int):
    If handle != __VD_STEN or handle < 1:
        vdTapeFault("vdom: vdTapeUnstash of " + "{handle}" + ", which is not the last tape stashed").
        Return.
    Set __VD_STEN to __VD_STEN - 1.
    vdAbort().
    vdDropPatches().
    Let base be __VD_STIN - 9.
    Let tpn be item (base + 1) of __VD_STI.
    Let on be item (base + 2) of __VD_STI.
    Let xn be item (base + 3) of __VD_STI.
    Let pwn be item (base + 4) of __VD_STI.
    Let tsn be item (base + 5) of __VD_STI.
    Let psn be item (base + 6) of __VD_STI.
    Let modok be item (base + 7) of __VD_STI.
    Let slots be item (base + 8) of __VD_STI.
    Let hydrating be item (base + 9) of __VD_STI.
    Let mutable at be base - pwn - 4 * xn - on - tpn.
    Set __VD_STIN to at.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= tpn:
        vdTapeInt(item (at + k) of __VD_STI).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set at to at + tpn.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= on:
        vdPushOpen(item (at + k) of __VD_STI).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set at to at + on.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= xn:
        Let x be at + 4 * (k - 1).
        vdPutSide(item (x + 1) of __VD_STI, item (x + 2) of __VD_STI, item (x + 3) of __VD_STI, item (x + 4) of __VD_STI).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set at to at + 4 * xn.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= pwn:
        vdEmitInt(item (at + k) of __VD_STI).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Let sbase be __VD_STSN - 1 - psn - tsn.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= tsn:
        Let restored be vdTapeStr(item (sbase + k) of __VD_STS).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= psn:
        Let emitted be vdEmitStr(item (sbase + tsn + k) of __VD_STS).
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set __VD_TAPEERR to item __VD_STSN of __VD_STS.
    Set __VD_STSN to sbase.
    Set __VD_MODOK to modok.
    Set __VD_SLOTS to slots.
    Set __VD_HYDRATING to hydrating.

## Note
Discards the tape being rendered — a failed render — leaving the retained tree and the stream untouched.

## To vdAbort():
    Set __VD_TPN to 0.
    Set __VD_TSN to 0.
    Set __VD_ON to 0.
    Set __VD_MODOK to 0.
    Set __VD_TAPEERR to "".
    Set __VD_SLOTS to 0.
    Set __VD_XN to 0.

## Note
The 1-based tape position just past the whole record starting at 1-based position `p`.

## To vdTapeSkip(p: Int) -> Int:
    Let op be item p of __VD_TP.
    If op == 1:
        Return (item (p + 3) of __VD_TP) + 1.
    If op == 5:
        Return (item (p + 2) of __VD_TP) + 1.
    If op == 15:
        Return (item (p + 1) of __VD_TP) + 1.
    If op == 10 or op == 13 or op == 17:
        Return p + 3.
    If op == 3 or op == 6 or op == 16:
        Return p + 1.
    Return p + 2.

## Note
The 1-based tape position where the children of the OPEN at 1-based position `p` start, past its modifier run.

## To vdChildrenStart(p: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable c be p + 4.
    Let mutable more be true.
    While more:
        Let op be item c of __VD_TP.
        If op == 10 or op == 13:
            Set c to c + 3.
        Otherwise If op == 9 or op == 11 or op == 12 or op == 14:
            Set c to c + 2.
        Otherwise:
            Set more to false.
    Return c.

## Note
True when the OPEN at 1-based tape position `p` sets raw html.

## To vdOpensHtml(p: Int) -> Bool:
    Let mutable c be p + 4.
    Let mutable more be true.
    While more:
        Let op be item c of __VD_TP.
        If op == 14:
            Return true.
        If op == 10 or op == 13:
            Set c to c + 3.
        Otherwise If op == 9 or op == 11 or op == 12:
            Set c to c + 2.
        Otherwise:
            Set more to false.
    Return false.

## Note
The key text the OPEN at 1-based tape position `p` carries.

## To vdTapeKey(p: Int) -> Text:
    Let at be item (p + 2) of __VD_TP.
    If at < 0:
        Return item (0 - at) of __VD_TS.
    Return item at of __VD_TS.

## Note
The tag the OPEN at 1-based tape position `p` names.

## To vdTapeTag(p: Int) -> Text:
    Return item (item (p + 1) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS.

## Note
A deterministic nonzero hash of `s`'s UTF-8 bytes, the same on every tier.

## To vdKeysHash(s: Text) -> Int:
    Let mutable h be 7.
    For each b in text_bytes(s):
        Set h to (h * 31 + b) % 1000000007.
    Return h + 1.

## Note
Writes slot `k` (1-based) of the sort scratch: entry `v` ordered by hash `h`.

## To vdPutSort(k: Int, v: Int, h: Int):
    If k > length of __VD_SORT:
        Push v to __VD_SORT.
        Push h to __VD_SORTH.
    Otherwise:
        Set item k of __VD_SORT to v.
        Set item k of __VD_SORTH to h.

## Note
True when sort slot `a` (1-based) orders before slot `b`: by hash, then by entry.

## To vdKeysSortBefore(a: Int, b: Int) -> Bool:
    Let ha be item a of __VD_SORTH.
    Let hb be item b of __VD_SORTH.
    If ha != hb:
        Return ha < hb.
    Return item a of __VD_SORT < item b of __VD_SORT.

## Note
Swaps sort slots `a` and `b` (1-based).

## To vdSortSwap(a: Int, b: Int):
    Let va be item a of __VD_SORT.
    Let ha be item a of __VD_SORTH.
    Set item a of __VD_SORT to item b of __VD_SORT.
    Set item a of __VD_SORTH to item b of __VD_SORTH.
    Set item b of __VD_SORT to va.
    Set item b of __VD_SORTH to ha.

## Note
Sifts 1-based sort slot `start` down a max-heap of the first `n` slots.

## To vdKeysSiftDown(start: Int, n: Int):
    Let mutable root be start.
    Let mutable going be true.
    While going:
        Let child be root * 2.
        If child > n:
            Set going to false.
        Otherwise:
            Let mutable big be child.
            If child + 1 <= n:
                If vdKeysSortBefore(child, child + 1):
                    Set big to child + 1.
            If vdKeysSortBefore(root, big):
                vdSortSwap(root, big).
                Set root to big.
            Otherwise:
                Set going to false.

## Note
Heap-sorts the first `n` sort slots by hash, then entry, in place.

## To vdKeysHeapSort(n: Int):
    Let mutable i be n / 2.
    While i >= 1:
        vdKeysSiftDown(i, n).
        Set i to i - 1.
    Let mutable last be n.
    While last > 1:
        vdSortSwap(1, last).
        Set last to last - 1.
        vdKeysSiftDown(1, last).

## Note
The first 1-based sort slot among the first `n` whose hash is at least `h`, or `n + 1`.

## To vdKeysSortSeek(h: Int, n: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable lo be 1.
    Let mutable hi be n + 1.
    While lo < hi:
        Let mid be (lo + hi) / 2.
        If item mid of __VD_SORTH < h:
            Set lo to mid + 1.
        Otherwise:
            Set hi to mid.
    Return lo.

## Note
Writes slot `k` (1-based) of the keyed-position scratch.

## To vdKeyedPut(k: Int, p: Int):
    If k > length of __VD_KP:
        Push p to __VD_KP.
    Otherwise:
        Set item k of __VD_KP to p.

## Note
The duplicate-key refusal naming `key` and both 1-based tape positions.

## To vdKeyedDuplicate(key: Text, first: Int, second: Int) -> Text:
    Return "vdom: duplicate key \"" + key + "\" on siblings at tape positions " + "{first}" + " and " + "{second}".

## Note
Refuses the first repeated key among the `n` keyed siblings in the keyed-position scratch, else `""`.

## To vdKeyedCheck(n: Int) -> Text:
    If n <= 32:
        Let mutable j be 2.
        While j <= n:
            Let pj be item j of __VD_KP.
            Let kj be vdTapeKey(pj).
            Let mutable i be 1.
            While i < j:
                Let earlier be item i of __VD_KP.
                If vdTapeKey(earlier) == kj:
                    Return vdKeyedDuplicate(kj, earlier, pj).
                Set i to i + 1.
            Set j to j + 1.
        Return "".
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= n:
        Let p be item k of __VD_KP.
        vdPutSort(k, p, vdKeysHash(vdTapeKey(p))).
        Set k to k + 1.
    vdKeysHeapSort(n).
    Let mutable bestFirst be 0.
    Let mutable bestSecond be 0.
    Let mutable bestKey be "".
    Let mutable runStart be 1.
    While runStart <= n:
        Let mutable runEnd be runStart.
        While runEnd < n and item (runEnd + 1) of __VD_SORTH == item runStart of __VD_SORTH:
            Set runEnd to runEnd + 1.
        Let mutable j be runStart + 1.
        While j <= runEnd:
            Let pj be item j of __VD_SORT.
            Let kj be vdTapeKey(pj).
            Let mutable i be runStart.
            Let mutable seeking be true.
            While seeking and i < j:
                Let earlier be item i of __VD_SORT.
                If vdTapeKey(earlier) == kj:
                    If bestSecond == 0 or pj < bestSecond:
                        Set bestFirst to earlier.
                        Set bestSecond to pj.
                        Set bestKey to kj.
                    Set seeking to false.
                Set i to i + 1.
            Set j to j + 1.
        Set runStart to runEnd + 1.
    If bestSecond != 0:
        Return vdKeyedDuplicate(bestKey, bestFirst, bestSecond).
    Return "".

## Note
Pushes one tape range onto the validation worklist.

## To vdPushRange(start: Int, end: Int):
    Set __VD_VN to __VD_VN + 1.
    If __VD_VN > length of __VD_VS:
        Push start to __VD_VS.
        Push end to __VD_VE.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_VN of __VD_VS to start.
        Set item __VD_VN of __VD_VE to end.

## Note
Everything `vdCommit` refuses before touching the tree: tape faults, an unclosed element, a bad target, duplicate keys or fragments, a keep of nothing.

## To vdValidate(target: Int) -> Text:
    If __VD_TAPEERR != "":
        Return __VD_TAPEERR.
    If __VD_ON > 0:
        Let p be item __VD_ON of __VD_OPENS.
        If item p of __VD_TP == 1:
            Return "vdom: <" + vdTapeTag(p) + "> was opened and never closed".
        Return "vdom: fragment " + "{item (p + 1) of __VD_TP}" + " was opened and never closed".
    If target < 1 or target >= length of __VD_KIND:
        Return "vdom: commit into node " + "{target}" + ", which does not exist".
    Let kind be item (target + 1) of __VD_KIND.
    If kind != 1 and kind != 3 and kind != 4:
        Return "vdom: commit into node " + "{target}" + ", which is not a root, element or fragment".
    If vdRealOf(target) == -1:
        Return "vdom: commit into fragment node " + "{target}" + ", which hangs from no host node".
    Set __VD_SERIAL to __VD_SERIAL + 1.
    Set __VD_VN to 0.
    vdPushRange(1, __VD_TPN + 1).
    While __VD_VN > 0:
        Let start be item __VD_VN of __VD_VS.
        Let end be item __VD_VN of __VD_VE.
        Set __VD_VN to __VD_VN - 1.
        Let mutable keyed be 0.
        Let mutable p be start.
        While p < end:
            Let op be item p of __VD_TP.
            If op == 1:
                If item (p + 2) of __VD_TP > 0 and vdTapeKey(p) != "":
                    Set keyed to keyed + 1.
                    vdKeyedPut(keyed, p).
                Let cs be vdChildrenStart(p).
                Let close be item (p + 3) of __VD_TP.
                If close <= p or close >= end:
                    Return "vdom: <" + vdTapeTag(p) + "> at tape position " + "{p}" + " is not closed inside its parent".
                If cs < close and vdOpensHtml(p):
                    Return "vdom: <" + vdTapeTag(p) + "> at tape position " + "{p}" + " sets raw html and also has children".
                vdPushRange(cs, close).
            Otherwise If op == 5 or op == 7:
                Let frag be item (p + 1) of __VD_TP.
                If frag < 1 or frag >= length of __VD_FRAGNODE:
                    Return "vdom: fragment " + "{frag}" + " was never made by vdNewFrag".
                If item (frag + 1) of __VD_WANT == __VD_SERIAL:
                    Return "vdom: fragment " + "{frag}" + " is placed twice in one render".
                Set item (frag + 1) of __VD_WANT to __VD_SERIAL.
                If op == 7:
                    If item (frag + 1) of __VD_FRAGNODE == 0:
                        Return "vdom: keep of fragment " + "{frag}" + ", which is not retained".
                Otherwise:
                    Let fragClose be item (p + 2) of __VD_TP.
                    If fragClose <= p or fragClose >= end:
                        Return "vdom: fragment " + "{frag}" + " at tape position " + "{p}" + " is not closed inside its parent".
                    vdPushRange(p + 3, fragClose).
            Otherwise If op != 2 and op != 17:
                Return "vdom: tape position " + "{p}" + " holds record " + "{op}" + " where a child belongs".
            Set p to vdTapeSkip(p).
        If keyed > 1:
            Let problem be vdKeyedCheck(keyed).
            If problem != "":
                Return problem.
    Return "".

## Note
Queues a diff of `parent`'s children against the 1-based tape range from `start` up to `end`.

## To vdPushWork(parent: Int, start: Int, end: Int):
    Set __VD_WN to __VD_WN + 1.
    If __VD_WN > length of __VD_WP:
        Push parent to __VD_WP.
        Push start to __VD_WS.
        Push end to __VD_WE.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_WN of __VD_WP to parent.
        Set item __VD_WN of __VD_WS to start.
        Set item __VD_WN of __VD_WE to end.

## Note
Marks `node` for release when the commit ends; nothing is freed while a later diff might still re-place a fragment.

## To vdDoom(node: Int):
    Set __VD_DOOMN to __VD_DOOMN + 1.
    If __VD_DOOMN > length of __VD_DOOM:
        Push node to __VD_DOOM.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_DOOMN of __VD_DOOM to node.

## Note
True when `node` is a fragment this commit's tape places again, so leaving here must not free it.

## To vdWanted(node: Int) -> Bool:
    If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
        Return false.
    Return item ((item (node + 1) of __VD_IDENT) + 1) of __VD_WANT == __VD_SERIAL.

## Note
Detaches every child of `node` and dooms each one this commit does not place again.

## To vdDoomChildren(node: Int):
    Let mutable c be item (node + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        Let nextC be item (c + 1) of __VD_NEXT.
        vdDetach(c).
        If not vdWanted(c):
            vdDoom(c).
        Set c to nextC.

## Note
Pushes `node` onto the node-walk scratch stack.

## To vdPushNode(node: Int):
    Set __VD_STKN to __VD_STKN + 1.
    If __VD_STKN > length of __VD_STK:
        Push node to __VD_STK.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_STKN of __VD_STK to node.

## Note
Frees `root` and every node under it, with an explicit stack rather than the call stack.

## To vdFreeSubtree(root: Int):
    Set __VD_STKN to 0.
    vdPushNode(root).
    While __VD_STKN > 0:
        Let node be item __VD_STKN of __VD_STK.
        Set __VD_STKN to __VD_STKN - 1.
        Let mutable c be item (node + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
        While c != -1:
            vdPushNode(c).
            Set c to item (c + 1) of __VD_NEXT.
        vdFree(node).

## Note
Emits one `FreeNode` per host node at the top of `node`'s range: `node` itself, or a fragment's real top-level descendants.

## To vdEmitFreeTops(node: Int):
    If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
        vdEmitFreeNode(node).
        Return.
    Let mutable c be item (node + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        If item (c + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
            vdEmitFreeNode(c).
            Set c to vdAfter(c, node).
        Otherwise:
            Let down be item (c + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
            If down != -1:
                Set c to down.
            Otherwise:
                Set c to vdAfter(c, node).

## Note
Emits `InsertBefore` for every host node at the top of `node`'s range, in order, under `host` before `next`.

## To vdMoveTops(node: Int, host: Int, next: Int):
    If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
        vdEmitInsertBefore(host, node, next).
        Return.
    Let mutable c be item (node + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        If item (c + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
            vdEmitInsertBefore(host, c, next).
            Set c to vdAfter(c, node).
        Otherwise:
            Let down be item (c + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
            If down != -1:
                Set c to down.
            Otherwise:
                Set c to vdAfter(c, node).

## Note
Frees every doomed node, emitting its `FreeNode`s after every create and move of the commit.

## To vdReleaseDoomed():
    Let mutable d be 1.
    While d <= __VD_DOOMN:
        Let node be item d of __VD_DOOM.
        vdEmitFreeTops(node).
        vdFreeSubtree(node).
        Set d to d + 1.
    Set __VD_DOOMN to 0.

## Note
The attribute entry on `node` named `name`, or `0`.

## To vdFindAttr(node: Int, name: Text) -> Int:
    Let mutable e be item (node + 1) of __VD_ATTR.
    While e != 0:
        If item (e + 1) of __VD_AN == name:
            Return e.
        Set e to item (e + 1) of __VD_ANEXT.
    Return 0.

## Note
Appends a new attribute `name`/`value` at the end of `node`'s chain, where a host puts a new attribute.

## To vdAddAttr(node: Int, name: Text, value: Text) -> Int:
    Let e be vdAttrAlloc(name, value).
    Let mutable last be item (node + 1) of __VD_ATTR.
    If last == 0:
        Set item (node + 1) of __VD_ATTR to e.
        Return e.
    While item (last + 1) of __VD_ANEXT != 0:
        Set last to item (last + 1) of __VD_ANEXT.
    Set item (last + 1) of __VD_ANEXT to e.
    Return e.

## Note
Removes, and emits `RemoveAttribute` for, every attribute of `node` the current modifier pass did not write.

## To vdSweepAttrs(node: Int):
    Let mutable prev be 0.
    Let mutable e be item (node + 1) of __VD_ATTR.
    While e != 0:
        Let nextE be item (e + 1) of __VD_ANEXT.
        If item (e + 1) of __VD_AMARK != __VD_MODN:
            vdEmitRemoveAttribute(node, item (e + 1) of __VD_AN).
            If prev == 0:
                Set item (node + 1) of __VD_ATTR to nextE.
            Otherwise:
                Set item (prev + 1) of __VD_ANEXT to nextE.
            vdAttrRelease(e).
        Otherwise:
            Set prev to e.
        Set e to nextE.

## Note
The listener entry on `node` for `event`, or `0`.

## To vdFindListen(node: Int, event: Text) -> Int:
    Let mutable e be item (node + 1) of __VD_LSN.
    While e != 0:
        If item (e + 1) of __VD_LE == event:
            Return e.
        Set e to item (e + 1) of __VD_LNEXT.
    Return 0.

## Note
Appends a new listener `event`/`flags` at the end of `node`'s chain.

## To vdAddListen(node: Int, event: Text, flags: Int) -> Int:
    Let e be vdListenAlloc(event, flags).
    Let mutable last be item (node + 1) of __VD_LSN.
    If last == 0:
        Set item (node + 1) of __VD_LSN to e.
        Return e.
    While item (last + 1) of __VD_LNEXT != 0:
        Set last to item (last + 1) of __VD_LNEXT.
    Set item (last + 1) of __VD_LNEXT to e.
    Return e.

## Note
Removes, and emits `Unlisten` for, every listener of `node` the current modifier pass did not write.

## To vdSweepListens(node: Int):
    Let mutable prev be 0.
    Let mutable e be item (node + 1) of __VD_LSN.
    While e != 0:
        Let nextE be item (e + 1) of __VD_LNEXT.
        If item (e + 1) of __VD_LMARK != __VD_MODN:
            vdEmitUnlisten(node, item (e + 1) of __VD_LE).
            If prev == 0:
                Set item (node + 1) of __VD_LSN to nextE.
            Otherwise:
                Set item (prev + 1) of __VD_LNEXT to nextE.
            vdListenRelease(e).
        Otherwise:
            Set prev to e.
        Set e to nextE.

## Note
Brings element `node` in line with the modifier run of the OPEN at 1-based tape position `p`; returns where its children start.

## To vdModifiers(node: Int, p: Int) -> Int:
    Let i be node + 1.
    Set __VD_MODN to __VD_MODN + 1.
    Let mutable sawHtml be false.
    Let mutable site be 0.
    Let mutable c be p + 4.
    Let mutable more be true.
    While more:
        Let op be item c of __VD_TP.
        If op == 10:
            Let name be item (item (c + 1) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS.
            Let value be item (item (c + 2) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS.
            Let mutable e be vdFindAttr(node, name).
            If e == 0:
                Set e to vdAddAttr(node, name, value).
                vdEmitSetAttribute(node, name, value).
            Otherwise If item (e + 1) of __VD_AV != value:
                Set item (e + 1) of __VD_AV to value.
                vdEmitSetAttribute(node, name, value).
            Set item (e + 1) of __VD_AMARK to __VD_MODN.
            Set c to c + 3.
        Otherwise If op == 11:
            Let value be item (item (c + 1) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS.
            Let flags be item i of __VD_FLAGS.
            If (flags & 1) == 0 or item i of __VD_VALUE != value:
                vdSetValueOf(node, value).
            Set item i of __VD_VALUE to value.
            Set item i of __VD_FLAGS to flags | 1.
            Set c to c + 2.
        Otherwise If op == 12:
            Let on be item (c + 1) of __VD_TP.
            Let flags be item i of __VD_FLAGS.
            Let mutable wasOn be 0.
            If (flags & 4) != 0:
                Set wasOn to 1.
            If (flags & 2) == 0 or wasOn != on:
                vdEmitSetChecked(node, on).
            If on == 1:
                Set item i of __VD_FLAGS to flags | 6.
            Otherwise:
                Set item i of __VD_FLAGS to (flags | 2) & 11.
            Set c to c + 2.
        Otherwise If op == 13:
            vdApplyListen(node, item (item (c + 1) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS, item (c + 2) of __VD_TP).
            Set c to c + 3.
        Otherwise If op == 14:
            Let markup be item (item (c + 1) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS.
            Set sawHtml to true.
            If item i of __VD_HTML != markup:
                vdEmitSetHtml(node, markup).
                Set item i of __VD_HTML to markup.
            Set c to c + 2.
        Otherwise If op == 9:
            Set site to item (c + 1) of __VD_TP.
            Set c to c + 2.
        Otherwise:
            Set more to false.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_XN:
        If item k of __VD_XP == p:
            If item k of __VD_XOP == 13:
                vdApplyListen(node, item (item k of __VD_XA) of __VD_TS, item k of __VD_XB).
            Otherwise:
                Set site to item k of __VD_XA.
        Set k to k + 1.
    vdSweepAttrs(node).
    vdSweepListens(node).
    If not sawHtml and item i of __VD_HTML != "":
        vdEmitSetHtml(node, "").
        Set item i of __VD_HTML to "".
    vdMarkSite(node, site).
    Return c.

## Note
Listens for `event` with `flags` on retained `node` this paint, emitting only what changed.

## To vdApplyListen(node: Int, event: Text, flags: Int):
    Let mutable e be vdFindListen(node, event).
    If e == 0:
        Set e to vdAddListen(node, event, flags).
        vdEmitListen(node, event, flags).
    Otherwise If item (e + 1) of __VD_LF != flags:
        Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LF to flags.
        vdEmitListen(node, event, flags).
    Set item (e + 1) of __VD_LMARK to __VD_MODN.

## Note
Makes `site` (or none, `0`) the site retained `node` carries after this paint.

## To vdMarkSite(node: Int, site: Int):
    Let i be node + 1.
    Let old be item i of __VD_SITE.
    If old != 0 and old != site:
        If item (old + 1) of __VD_SITENODE == node:
            Set item (old + 1) of __VD_SITENODE to 0.
    Set item i of __VD_SITE to site.
    If site != 0:
        vdPutSiteNode(site, node).

## Note
Makes a fresh node for the tape record at 1-based position `p`, emits its creation, and queues its children.

## To vdMount(p: Int) -> Int:
    Let op be item p of __VD_TP.
    Let node be vdAlloc().
    Let i be node + 1.
    If op == 2 or op == 17:
        Let text be item (item (p + 1) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS.
        Set item i of __VD_KIND to 2.
        Set item i of __VD_TEXT to text.
        vdEmitCreateText(node, text).
        If op == 17:
            vdMarkSite(node, item (p + 2) of __VD_TP).
        Return node.
    If op == 5:
        Let frag be item (p + 1) of __VD_TP.
        Set item i of __VD_KIND to 3.
        Set item i of __VD_IDENT to frag.
        Set item (frag + 1) of __VD_FRAGNODE to node.
        vdPushWork(node, p + 3, item (p + 2) of __VD_TP).
        Return node.
    Let tag be vdTapeTag(p).
    Set item i of __VD_KIND to 1.
    Set item i of __VD_TAG to tag.
    Set item i of __VD_KEY to vdTapeKey(p).
    vdEmitCreateElement(node, tag).
    Let cs be vdModifiers(node, p).
    If item i of __VD_HTML == "":
        vdPushWork(node, cs, item (p + 3) of __VD_TP).
    Return node.

## Note
Reuses `node` for the tape record at 1-based position `p`: emits what changed and queues its children.

## To vdPatch(node: Int, p: Int):
    Let op be item p of __VD_TP.
    Let i be node + 1.
    If op == 2 or op == 17:
        Let text be item (item (p + 1) of __VD_TP) of __VD_TS.
        If item i of __VD_TEXT != text:
            Set item i of __VD_TEXT to text.
            vdEmitSetText(node, text).
        If op == 17:
            vdMarkSite(node, item (p + 2) of __VD_TP).
        Otherwise:
            vdMarkSite(node, 0).
        Return.
    If op == 5:
        vdPushWork(node, p + 3, item (p + 2) of __VD_TP).
        Return.
    If op == 7:
        Return.
    Let cs be vdModifiers(node, p).
    If item i of __VD_HTML == "":
        vdPushWork(node, cs, item (p + 3) of __VD_TP).
    Otherwise:
        vdDoomChildren(node).

## Note
True when retained `node` is the same child as the tape record at 1-based position `p`: one fragment, or one kind, tag and key.

## To vdSame(node: Int, p: Int) -> Bool:
    Let op be item p of __VD_TP.
    Let kind be item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND.
    If op == 5 or op == 7:
        Return kind == 3 and item (node + 1) of __VD_IDENT == item (p + 1) of __VD_TP.
    If op == 2 or op == 17:
        Return kind == 2.
    If kind != 1:
        Return false.
    Return item (node + 1) of __VD_TAG == vdTapeTag(p) and item (node + 1) of __VD_KEY == vdTapeKey(p).

## Note
The tag positional matching compares an unkeyed retained `node` by.

## To vdMatchTag(node: Int) -> Text:
    Let kind be item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND.
    If kind == 1:
        Return item (node + 1) of __VD_TAG.
    If kind == 2:
        Return "#text".
    Return "#fragment".

## Note
Writes 1-based slot `k` of the retained-children scratch.

## To vdPutR(k: Int, node: Int):
    If k > length of __VD_R:
        Push node to __VD_R.
    Otherwise:
        Set item k of __VD_R to node.

## Note
Writes 1-based fresh slot `k`: tape position `p`, no match yet.

## To vdPutFresh(k: Int, p: Int):
    If k > length of __VD_F:
        Push p to __VD_F.
        Push 0 to __VD_M.
        Push 0 to __VD_KJ.
    Otherwise:
        Set item k of __VD_F to p.
        Set item k of __VD_M to 0.
        Set item k of __VD_KJ to 0.

## Note
Pairs 1-based fresh slot `j` with `node` in `state` (0 matched, 1 in place, 2 new, 3 re-placed from elsewhere).

## To vdMatch(j: Int, node: Int, state: Int, serial: Int):
    Set item j of __VD_M to node.
    Set item j of __VD_KJ to state.
    Set item (node + 1) of __VD_MARK to serial.

## Note
Writes 1-based slot `k` of the cursor scratch: positional matching for `tag` resumes at retained slot `at`.

## To vdPutCursor(k: Int, tag: Text, at: Int):
    If k > length of __VD_CT:
        Push tag to __VD_CT.
        Push at to __VD_CP.
    Otherwise:
        Set item k of __VD_CT to tag.
        Set item k of __VD_CP to at.

## Note
The key hash of retained `node`, computed once and kept.

## To vdKeysNodeHash(node: Int) -> Int:
    Let h be item (node + 1) of __VD_KH.
    If h != 0:
        Return h.
    Let fresh be vdKeysHash(item (node + 1) of __VD_KEY).
    Set item (node + 1) of __VD_KH to fresh.
    Return fresh.

## Note
Sorts the keyed elements among retained slots from 1-based `lo` to `hi` by key hash; returns how many.

## To vdKeysSortRetained(lo: Int, hi: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable n be 0.
    Let mutable ri be lo.
    While ri <= hi:
        Let node be item ri of __VD_R.
        If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND == 1 and item (node + 1) of __VD_KEY != "":
            Set n to n + 1.
            vdPutSort(n, node, vdKeysNodeHash(node)).
        Set ri to ri + 1.
    vdKeysHeapSort(n).
    Return n.

## Note
The unmatched retained element keyed `key` with tag `tag` among retained slots `lo` to `hi` (1-based), or `0`.

## To vdKeysFind(key: Text, tag: Text, lo: Int, hi: Int, sorted: Int, serial: Int) -> Int:
    If sorted < 0:
        Let mutable ri be lo.
        While ri <= hi:
            Let node be item ri of __VD_R.
            If item (node + 1) of __VD_MARK != serial and item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND == 1:
                If item (node + 1) of __VD_KEY == key and item (node + 1) of __VD_TAG == tag:
                    Return node.
            Set ri to ri + 1.
        Return 0.
    Let h be vdKeysHash(key).
    Let mutable k be vdKeysSortSeek(h, sorted).
    While k <= sorted:
        If item k of __VD_SORTH != h:
            Return 0.
        Let node be item k of __VD_SORT.
        If item (node + 1) of __VD_MARK != serial and item (node + 1) of __VD_KEY == key and item (node + 1) of __VD_TAG == tag:
            Return node.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return 0.

## Note
The unmatched unkeyed retained child with match tag `tag`, scanning slots up to `hi` from where the last match of that tag stopped.

## To vdFindPositional(tag: Text, lo: Int, hi: Int, cursors: Int, serial: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable slot be 0.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= cursors:
        If item k of __VD_CT == tag:
            Set slot to k.
            Set k to cursors.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Let mutable ri be lo.
    If slot != 0:
        Set ri to item slot of __VD_CP.
    Let mutable found be 0.
    While ri <= hi and found == 0:
        Let node be item ri of __VD_R.
        If item (node + 1) of __VD_MARK != serial and item (node + 1) of __VD_KEY == "" and item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
            If vdMatchTag(node) == tag:
                Set found to node.
        Set ri to ri + 1.
    If slot == 0:
        vdPutCursor(cursors + 1, tag, ri).
    Otherwise:
        Set item slot of __VD_CP to ri.
    Return found.

## Note
Writes 1-based slot `k` of the reorder scratch: retained position `pos` of fresh slot `j`.

## To vdPutSeq(k: Int, pos: Int, j: Int):
    If k > length of __VD_SEQ:
        Push pos to __VD_SEQ.
        Push j to __VD_SEQJ.
        Push 0 to __VD_LKEEP.
        Push 0 to __VD_TAILS.
        Push -1 to __VD_PREVI.
    Otherwise:
        Set item k of __VD_SEQ to pos.
        Set item k of __VD_SEQJ to j.

## Note
Marks, over reorder slots 1 to `n` (1-based), a longest strictly increasing run of retained positions: those children stay put.

## To vdLis(n: Int):
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i <= n:
        Set item i of __VD_LKEEP to 0.
        Set item i of __VD_PREVI to -1.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Let mutable tails be 0.
    Set i to 1.
    While i <= n:
        Let vi be item i of __VD_SEQ.
        Let mutable lo be 1.
        Let mutable hi be tails + 1.
        While lo < hi:
            Let mid be (lo + hi) / 2.
            If item (item mid of __VD_TAILS) of __VD_SEQ < vi:
                Set lo to mid + 1.
            Otherwise:
                Set hi to mid.
        If lo > 1:
            Set item i of __VD_PREVI to item (lo - 1) of __VD_TAILS.
        If lo > tails:
            Set tails to tails + 1.
        Set item lo of __VD_TAILS to i.
        Set i to i + 1.
    If tails == 0:
        Return.
    Let mutable cursor be item tails of __VD_TAILS.
    While cursor != -1:
        Set item cursor of __VD_LKEEP to 1.
        Set cursor to item cursor of __VD_PREVI.

## Note
Which 1-based entries of `seq` lie on a longest strictly increasing run (1) and which must move (0).

## To vdLongestIncreasingRun(seq: Seq of Int) -> Seq of Int:
    Let n be length of seq.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= n:
        vdPutSeq(k, item k of seq, k).
        Set k to k + 1.
    vdLis(n).
    Let out be a new Seq of Int.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= n:
        Push (item k of __VD_LKEEP) to out.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return out.

## Note
Links fresh slots 1 to `f` (1-based) under `parent` as its children, in order.

## To vdRelink(parent: Int, f: Int):
    Let mutable prev be -1.
    Let mutable j be 1.
    While j <= f:
        Let node be item j of __VD_M.
        Set item (node + 1) of __VD_PARENT to parent.
        Set item (node + 1) of __VD_PREV to prev.
        If prev == -1:
            Set item (parent + 1) of __VD_FIRST to node.
        Otherwise:
            Set item (prev + 1) of __VD_NEXT to node.
        Set prev to node.
        Set j to j + 1.
    If prev == -1:
        Set item (parent + 1) of __VD_FIRST to -1.
    Otherwise:
        Set item (prev + 1) of __VD_NEXT to -1.
    Set item (parent + 1) of __VD_LAST to prev.

## Note
Diffs `parent`'s children against the fresh tape range from 1-based `start` up to `end`, queuing their own children.

## To vdDiff(parent: Int, start: Int, end: Int):
    Set __VD_DIFFN to __VD_DIFFN + 1.
    Let serial be __VD_DIFFN.
    Let mutable r be 0.
    Let mutable c be item (parent + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        Set r to r + 1.
        vdPutR(r, c).
        Set item (c + 1) of __VD_POS to r.
        Set c to item (c + 1) of __VD_NEXT.
    Let mutable f be 0.
    Let mutable p be start.
    While p < end:
        Set f to f + 1.
        vdPutFresh(f, p).
        Set p to vdTapeSkip(p).
    Let mutable h be 0.
    Let mutable trimming be true.
    While trimming:
        If h >= r or h >= f:
            Set trimming to false.
        Otherwise If vdSame(item (h + 1) of __VD_R, item (h + 1) of __VD_F):
            Set h to h + 1.
            vdMatch(h, item h of __VD_R, 1, serial).
        Otherwise:
            Set trimming to false.
    Let mutable t be 0.
    Set trimming to true.
    While trimming:
        If h + t >= r or h + t >= f:
            Set trimming to false.
        Otherwise If vdSame(item (r - t) of __VD_R, item (f - t) of __VD_F):
            vdMatch(f - t, item (r - t) of __VD_R, 1, serial).
            Set t to t + 1.
        Otherwise:
            Set trimming to false.
    Let lo be h + 1.
    Let hiR be r - t.
    Let hiF be f - t.
    Let mutable sorted be -1.
    If hiR - lo + 1 > 32:
        Set sorted to -2.
    Let mutable cursors be 0.
    Let mutable fj be lo.
    While fj <= hiF:
        Let fp be item fj of __VD_F.
        Let op be item fp of __VD_TP.
        If op == 5 or op == 7:
            Let node be item ((item (fp + 1) of __VD_TP) + 1) of __VD_FRAGNODE.
            If node != 0:
                If item (node + 1) of __VD_PARENT == parent and item (node + 1) of __VD_MARK != serial:
                    vdMatch(fj, node, 0, serial).
                Otherwise:
                    vdDetach(node).
                    vdMatch(fj, node, 3, serial).
        Otherwise If op == 1 and vdTapeKey(fp) != "":
            If sorted == -2:
                Set sorted to vdKeysSortRetained(lo, hiR).
            Let found be vdKeysFind(vdTapeKey(fp), vdTapeTag(fp), lo, hiR, sorted, serial).
            If found != 0:
                vdMatch(fj, found, 0, serial).
        Otherwise:
            Let mutable tag be "#text".
            If op == 1:
                Set tag to vdTapeTag(fp).
            Let found be vdFindPositional(tag, lo, hiR, cursors, serial).
            Set cursors to length of __VD_CT.
            If found != 0:
                vdMatch(fj, found, 0, serial).
        Set fj to fj + 1.
    Let mutable ri be lo.
    While ri <= hiR:
        Let gone be item ri of __VD_R.
        If item (gone + 1) of __VD_MARK != serial:
            vdDetach(gone).
            If not vdWanted(gone):
                vdDoom(gone).
        Set ri to ri + 1.
    Set fj to 1.
    While fj <= f:
        Let node be item fj of __VD_M.
        If node == 0:
            vdMatch(fj, vdMount(item fj of __VD_F), 2, serial).
        Otherwise:
            vdPatch(node, item fj of __VD_F).
        Set fj to fj + 1.
    Let mutable n be 0.
    Set fj to lo.
    While fj <= hiF:
        If item fj of __VD_KJ == 0:
            Set n to n + 1.
            vdPutSeq(n, item ((item fj of __VD_M) + 1) of __VD_POS, fj).
        Set fj to fj + 1.
    vdLis(n).
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= n:
        If item k of __VD_LKEEP == 1:
            Set item (item k of __VD_SEQJ) of __VD_KJ to 1.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Let host be vdRealOf(parent).
    Let mutable next be -1.
    If item (parent + 1) of __VD_KIND == 3:
        Set next to vdAnchorAfter(parent).
    Let mutable tail be f + 1.
    If next == -1:
        While tail > 1 and item (tail - 1) of __VD_KJ == 2:
            Set tail to tail - 1.
        Set fj to tail.
        While fj <= f:
            Let node be item fj of __VD_M.
            If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
                vdEmitAppendChild(host, node).
                If next == -1:
                    Set next to node.
            Set fj to fj + 1.
    Set fj to tail - 1.
    While fj >= 1:
        Let node be item fj of __VD_M.
        Let state be item fj of __VD_KJ.
        If state == 2:
            If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND != 3:
                If next == -1:
                    vdEmitAppendChild(host, node).
                Otherwise:
                    vdEmitInsertBefore(host, node, next).
        Otherwise If state == 0 or state == 3:
            vdMoveTops(node, host, next).
        Let first be vdFirstReal(node).
        If first != -1:
            Set next to first.
        Set fj to fj - 1.
    vdRelink(parent, f).

## Note
Appends word `v` to the resolved tape `vdSlotsResolve` builds.

## To vdSlotsTqInt(v: Int):
    Set __VD_TQN to __VD_TQN + 1.
    If __VD_TQN > length of __VD_TQ:
        Push v to __VD_TQ.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_TQN of __VD_TQ to v.

## Note
Pushes the 1-based position of an OPEN or FRAG_OPEN just copied, whose end is written when its close is.

## To vdSlotsPushReloc(q: Int):
    Set __VD_RELOCN to __VD_RELOCN + 1.
    If __VD_RELOCN > length of __VD_RELOC:
        Push q to __VD_RELOC.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_RELOCN of __VD_RELOC to q.

## Note
Pushes the tape segment from `start` up to `end` to be copied next.

## To vdSlotsPushSeg(start: Int, end: Int):
    Set __VD_SEGN to __VD_SEGN + 1.
    If __VD_SEGN > length of __VD_SEGS:
        Push start to __VD_SEGS.
        Push end to __VD_SEGE.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_SEGN of __VD_SEGS to start.
        Set item __VD_SEGN of __VD_SEGE to end.

## Note
Copies every range into the slot that places it, so the tape every later step reads holds no slot.
Answers `""`, or why the tape cannot be resolved.

## To vdSlotsResolve() -> Text:
    If __VD_TAPEERR != "":
        Return __VD_TAPEERR.
    Set __VD_TQN to 0.
    Set __VD_RELOCN to 0.
    Set __VD_SEGN to 0.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= __VD_XN:
        Set item k of __VD_XQ to 0.
        Set k to k + 1.
    vdSlotsPushSeg(1, __VD_TPN + 1).
    Let mutable placed be 0.
    While __VD_SEGN > 0:
        Let p be item __VD_SEGN of __VD_SEGS.
        Let end be item __VD_SEGN of __VD_SEGE.
        If p >= end:
            Set __VD_SEGN to __VD_SEGN - 1.
        Otherwise:
            Let op be item p of __VD_TP.
            Let after be vdTapeSkipRecord(p).
            Set item __VD_SEGN of __VD_SEGS to after.
            If op == 15:
                Set item __VD_SEGN of __VD_SEGS to (item (p + 1) of __VD_TP) + 1.
            Otherwise If op == 8:
                Let range be item (p + 1) of __VD_TP.
                If range < 1 or range > __VD_TPN or item range of __VD_TP != 15:
                    Return "vdom: a slot names tape position " + "{range}" + ", which opens no range".
                Set placed to placed + 1.
                If placed > __VD_TPN:
                    Return "vdom: a slot places a range inside itself".
                vdSlotsPushSeg(range + 2, item (range + 1) of __VD_TP).
            Otherwise If op != 16:
                Let q be __VD_TQN + 1.
                Let mutable w be p.
                While w < after:
                    vdSlotsTqInt(item w of __VD_TP).
                    Set w to w + 1.
                If op == 1:
                    vdSlotsPushReloc(q).
                    Set k to 1.
                    While k <= __VD_XN:
                        If item k of __VD_XP == p:
                            Set item k of __VD_XQ to q.
                        Set k to k + 1.
                Otherwise If op == 5:
                    vdSlotsPushReloc(q).
                Otherwise If op == 3:
                    Let o be item __VD_RELOCN of __VD_RELOC.
                    Set __VD_RELOCN to __VD_RELOCN - 1.
                    Set item (o + 3) of __VD_TQ to q.
                Otherwise If op == 6:
                    Let o be item __VD_RELOCN of __VD_RELOC.
                    Set __VD_RELOCN to __VD_RELOCN - 1.
                    Set item (o + 2) of __VD_TQ to q.
    Let resolved be __VD_TQ.
    Set __VD_TQ to __VD_TP.
    Set __VD_TP to resolved.
    Set __VD_TPN to __VD_TQN.
    Set k to 1.
    While k <= __VD_XN:
        Set item k of __VD_XP to item k of __VD_XQ.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Set __VD_SLOTS to 0.
    Return "".

## Note
The 1-based tape position just past the ONE record at `p` — an OPEN's header or a FRAG_OPEN's, not the subtree behind it.

## To vdTapeSkipRecord(p: Int) -> Int:
    Let op be item p of __VD_TP.
    If op == 1:
        Return p + 4.
    If op == 5 or op == 10 or op == 13 or op == 17:
        Return p + 3.
    If op == 3 or op == 6 or op == 16:
        Return p + 1.
    Return p + 2.

## Note
Diffs the tape against `node`'s retained children and appends the minimal patch stream; answers
`""`, or the refusal with the tree untouched.

## To vdCommit(node: Int) -> Text:
    If __VD_SLOTS != 0:
        Let resolveProblem be vdSlotsResolve().
        If resolveProblem != "":
            vdAbort().
            Return resolveProblem.
    Let problem be vdValidate(node).
    If problem != "":
        vdAbort().
        Return problem.
    Let mutable adopting be false.
    If ((item (node + 1) of __VD_FLAGS) & 16) != 0:
        Set item (node + 1) of __VD_FLAGS to (item (node + 1) of __VD_FLAGS) - 16.
        Set adopting to item (node + 1) of __VD_FIRST == -1.
    Let wordsBefore be __VD_PWN.
    Let stringsBefore be __VD_PSN.
    Set __VD_WN to 0.
    Set __VD_DOOMN to 0.
    vdPushWork(node, 1, __VD_TPN + 1).
    While __VD_WN > 0:
        Let parent be item __VD_WN of __VD_WP.
        Let start be item __VD_WN of __VD_WS.
        Let end be item __VD_WN of __VD_WE.
        Set __VD_WN to __VD_WN - 1.
        vdDiff(parent, start, end).
    vdEmitLate().
    vdReleaseDoomed().
    If adopting:
        Set __VD_PWN to wordsBefore.
        Set __VD_PSN to stringsBefore.
        vdAdoptTree(node, true).
        Set __VD_HYDRATING to node.
    Set __VD_TPN to 0.
    Set __VD_TSN to 0.
    Set __VD_XN to 0.
    Return "".

## Note
True when `tag` names a void element, which has no content and no closing tag.

## To vdIsVoid(tag: Text) -> Bool:
    Return vdTagIn(tag, "area base br col embed hr img input link meta param source track wbr").

## Note
True when `tag` names a raw text element, whose text is not markup.

## To vdIsRawText(tag: Text) -> Bool:
    Return vdTagIn(tag, "style script").

## Note
True when `tag`, compared without ASCII case, is one of the space-separated lowercase `names`.

## To vdTagIn(tag: Text, names: Text) -> Bool:
    Let bytes be text_bytes(tag).
    Let n be length of bytes.
    Let list be text_bytes(names).
    Let total be length of list.
    Let mutable at be 1.
    While at <= total:
        Let mutable stop be at.
        While stop <= total and item stop of list != 32:
            Set stop to stop + 1.
        If stop - at == n:
            Let mutable same be true.
            Let mutable k be 1.
            While same and k <= n:
                Let mutable b be item k of bytes.
                If b >= 65 and b <= 90:
                    Set b to b + 32.
                If b != item (at + k - 1) of list:
                    Set same to false.
                Set k to k + 1.
            If same:
                Return true.
        Set at to stop + 1.
    Return false.

## Note
`s` escaped for an HTML text node (`&`, `<`, `>`), or for an attribute value too when `quote` (`"` as well).

## To vdEscape(s: Text, quote: Bool) -> Text:
    Let mutable out be "".
    For each ch in s:
        If ch == "&":
            Set out to out + "&amp;".
        Otherwise If ch == "<":
            Set out to out + "&lt;".
        Otherwise If ch == ">":
            Set out to out + "&gt;".
        Otherwise If quote and ch == "\"":
            Set out to out + "&quot;".
        Otherwise:
            Set out to out + ch.
    Return out.

## Note
True when text `a` sorts before `b` byte by byte, the order a host lists attributes in.

## To vdBytesBefore(a: Text, b: Text) -> Bool:
    Let x be text_bytes(a).
    Let y be text_bytes(b).
    Let nx be length of x.
    Let ny be length of y.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k <= nx and k <= ny:
        If item k of x != item k of y:
            Return item k of x < item k of y.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return nx < ny.

## Note
`node`'s attributes as markup, sorted by name the way a host serializes them.

## To vdAttrMarkup(node: Int) -> Text:
    Let mutable n be 0.
    Let mutable e be item (node + 1) of __VD_ATTR.
    While e != 0:
        Set n to n + 1.
        vdPutSort(n, e, 0).
        Set e to item (e + 1) of __VD_ANEXT.
    Let mutable j be 2.
    While j <= n:
        Let mutable k be j.
        While k > 1 and vdBytesBefore(item ((item k of __VD_SORT) + 1) of __VD_AN, item ((item (k - 1) of __VD_SORT) + 1) of __VD_AN):
            vdSortSwap(k, k - 1).
            Set k to k - 1.
        Set j to j + 1.
    Let mutable out be "".
    Set j to 1.
    While j <= n:
        Let a be item j of __VD_SORT.
        Set out to out + " " + item (a + 1) of __VD_AN + "=\"" + vdEscape(item (a + 1) of __VD_AV, true) + "\"".
        Set j to j + 1.
    Return out.

## Note
The text content of `node`: every text node under it, in order.

## To vdTextContent(node: Int) -> Text:
    If item (node + 1) of __VD_KIND == 2:
        Return item (node + 1) of __VD_TEXT.
    Let mutable out be "".
    Let mutable c be item (node + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        If item (c + 1) of __VD_KIND == 2:
            Set out to out + item (c + 1) of __VD_TEXT.
            Set c to vdAfter(c, node).
        Otherwise:
            Let down be item (c + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
            If down != -1:
                Set c to down.
            Otherwise:
                Set c to vdAfter(c, node).
    Return out.

## Note
The value `select` shows before anyone chooses: its `selected` option's, else its first option's (an option's value attribute, else its text).

## To vdDefaultChoice(select: Int) -> Text:
    Let mutable first be "".
    Let mutable seen be false.
    Let mutable c be item (select + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        Let mutable descend be true.
        If item (c + 1) of __VD_KIND == 1:
            If vdTagIn(item (c + 1) of __VD_TAG, "option"):
                Set descend to false.
                Let mutable value be vdTextContent(c).
                Let v be vdFindAttr(c, "value").
                If v != 0:
                    Set value to item (v + 1) of __VD_AV.
                If vdFindAttr(c, "selected") != 0:
                    Return value.
                If not seen:
                    Set first to value.
                    Set seen to true.
        Let down be item (c + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
        If descend and down != -1:
            Set c to down.
        Otherwise:
            Set c to vdAfter(c, select).
    Return first.

## Note
Pushes `node` at walk `phase` onto the serializer's stack.

## To vdPushSerial(node: Int, phase: Int):
    Set __VD_SNN to __VD_SNN + 1.
    If __VD_SNN > length of __VD_SN:
        Push node to __VD_SN.
        Push phase to __VD_SPH.
    Otherwise:
        Set item __VD_SNN of __VD_SN to node.
        Set item __VD_SNN of __VD_SPH to phase.

## Note
Pushes `node`'s children onto the serializer's stack so the first comes off first.

## To vdPushChildren(node: Int):
    Let mutable c be item (node + 1) of __VD_LAST.
    While c != -1:
        vdPushSerial(c, 0).
        Set c to item (c + 1) of __VD_PREV.

## Note
`node` rendered to markup as a host serializes it — an element with its tag, a fragment or root as its children.

## To vdSerialize(node: Int) -> Text:
    Let mutable out be "".
    Set __VD_SNN to 0.
    vdPushSerial(node, 0).
    While __VD_SNN > 0:
        Let n be item __VD_SNN of __VD_SN.
        Let phase be item __VD_SNN of __VD_SPH.
        Set __VD_SNN to __VD_SNN - 1.
        Let i be n + 1.
        Let kind be item i of __VD_KIND.
        If kind == 2:
            Let up be vdRealOf(item i of __VD_PARENT).
            If up != -1 and item (up + 1) of __VD_KIND == 1 and vdIsRawText(item (up + 1) of __VD_TAG):
                Set out to out + item i of __VD_TEXT.
            Otherwise:
                Set out to out + vdEscape(item i of __VD_TEXT, false).
        Otherwise If kind == 1 and phase == 1:
            Set out to out + "</" + item i of __VD_TAG + ">".
        Otherwise If kind == 1:
            Let tag be item i of __VD_TAG.
            Set out to out + "<" + tag + vdAttrMarkup(n).
            Let flags be item i of __VD_FLAGS.
            If (flags & 4) != 0:
                Set out to out + " checked".
            Let value be item i of __VD_VALUE.
            If value != "":
                If not vdTagIn(tag, "select") or vdDefaultChoice(n) != value:
                    Set out to out + " value=\"" + vdEscape(value, true) + "\"".
            Set out to out + ">".
            If not vdIsVoid(tag):
                Set out to out + item i of __VD_HTML.
                vdPushSerial(n, 1).
                vdPushChildren(n).
        Otherwise:
            vdPushChildren(n).
    Return out.

## Note
Every child of `node` rendered to markup, in order.

## To vdSerializeChildren(node: Int) -> Text:
    Let mutable out be "".
    Let mutable c be item (node + 1) of __VD_FIRST.
    While c != -1:
        Set out to out + vdSerialize(c).
        Set c to item (c + 1) of __VD_NEXT.
    Return out.
